WEBVTT

1
00:03:00.792 --> 00:03:02.375
Star.

2
00:03:05.917 --> 00:03:07.583
Comm… Command.

3
00:03:11.125 --> 00:03:12.333
Star.

4
00:03:12.917 --> 00:03:14.291
Command.

5
00:03:14.292 --> 00:03:17.457
Star. Command.

6
00:03:17.458 --> 00:03:18.832
- Rendezvous!
- With!

7
00:03:18.833 --> 00:03:20.041
Star Command.

8
00:03:20.042 --> 00:03:38.333
Rendezvous with Star Command.

9
00:04:00.042 --> 00:04:01.167
There.

10
00:04:03.250 --> 00:04:06.208
This way, you'll never lose me, Jessie.

11
00:04:07.750 --> 00:04:10.249
Friends forever, partner.

12
00:04:11.458 --> 00:04:13.207
That's right, partner.

13
00:04:13.208 --> 00:04:16.541
But don't you worry.
I'll keep a good eye on you.

14
00:04:19.542 --> 00:04:22.457
See? I'm still watching.

15
00:04:23.750 --> 00:04:26.749
I'm gone… …but I'm back.

16
00:04:26.750 --> 00:04:29.708
I'm gone. I'm back.

17
00:04:30.250 --> 00:04:32.291
I still see you.

18
00:04:32.292 --> 00:04:35.083
Oh, no. I'm gone.

19
00:04:37.583 --> 00:04:40.707
And I will love you all the time…

20
00:04:40.708 --> 00:04:43.957
even when I'm mad or sad

21
00:04:43.958 --> 00:04:46.124
or leave you outside by accident.

22
00:04:46.125 --> 00:04:48.167
I'll still love you forever.

23
00:04:48.917 --> 00:04:50.499
Really? You mean it?

24
00:04:50.500 --> 00:04:52.207
Forever and ever and ever?

25
00:04:52.208 --> 00:04:54.707
Yep. All the evers.

26
00:04:54.708 --> 00:04:57.791
Then do you, Forky, take Karen Beverly

27
00:04:57.792 --> 00:05:00.124
to be your beloved bride?

28
00:05:00.125 --> 00:05:01.499
I do.

29
00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:03.332
And do you, Karen Beverly?

30
00:05:03.333 --> 00:05:04.499
I do.

31
00:05:09.167 --> 00:05:11.207
Yeehaw!

32
00:05:11.208 --> 00:05:13.707
I now pronounce you husband…

33
00:05:13.708 --> 00:05:15.750
and knife.

34
00:05:18.250 --> 00:05:19.874
Kissy, kissy.

35
00:05:25.458 --> 00:05:28.207
Who poisoned the maid of honor?

36
00:05:32.792 --> 00:05:38.249
Oh! Why? Why?

37
00:05:38.250 --> 00:05:39.458
Everyone!

38
00:05:40.083 --> 00:05:42.874
Step aside. I know CPR.

39
00:05:42.875 --> 00:05:44.625
One, two, three.

40
00:05:45.125 --> 00:05:48.332
Now, the kiss of life.

41
00:05:55.958 --> 00:05:57.041
Oh.

42
00:06:04.708 --> 00:06:06.667
You're so funny.

43
00:06:09.917 --> 00:06:11.957
But we didn't solve my murder.

44
00:06:11.958 --> 00:06:14.249
Just hold your horses, Rex.

45
00:06:14.250 --> 00:06:16.041
Psst. Dolly, what's going on?

46
00:06:16.042 --> 00:06:17.832
Not sure.

47
00:06:17.833 --> 00:06:19.207
You know, at first I was mad

48
00:06:19.208 --> 00:06:20.499
Bonnie drew these glasses on me,

49
00:06:20.500 --> 00:06:22.416
but honestly, I can see
so much better now.

50
00:06:22.417 --> 00:06:23.999
Dolly, focus.

51
00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:25.082
Oh! Sorry.

52
00:06:25.083 --> 00:06:27.291
It's the Jordan twins. They're back home.

53
00:06:33.833 --> 00:06:37.000
Poor thing. She's still afraid
to ask them to play.

54
00:06:37.792 --> 00:06:39.500
Not this time.

55
00:06:44.458 --> 00:06:46.874
Giddy-up there! Time's a-wastin'!

56
00:06:46.875 --> 00:06:48.125
Oh, no.

57
00:06:58.083 --> 00:06:59.832
That's it, Bonnie.

58
00:06:59.833 --> 00:07:01.083
You can do it.

59
00:07:14.750 --> 00:07:17.083
Hello.

60
00:07:30.292 --> 00:07:32.457
Uh, Jessie. The wedding got me thinking…

61
00:07:32.458 --> 00:07:33.874
Shh. Something's off.

62
00:07:33.875 --> 00:07:36.082
So, how'd the wedding go?

63
00:07:36.083 --> 00:07:37.749
Who murdered the maid of honor this time?

64
00:07:37.750 --> 00:07:39.957
Mom? Dad?

65
00:07:39.958 --> 00:07:41.167
Yeah, sweetie?

66
00:07:43.083 --> 00:07:45.832
Why won't anyone be my friend?

67
00:07:47.292 --> 00:07:50.167
- Oh, Bonnie, come here.
- Oh, sweetie.

68
00:07:55.417 --> 00:07:57.124
- Buzz.
- Ow.

69
00:07:57.125 --> 00:07:58.791
You're deputy till I get back.

70
00:07:58.792 --> 00:07:59.957
Me? Right.

71
00:07:59.958 --> 00:08:03.416
I'm gonna get those twins
to play with Bonnie somehow.

72
00:08:03.417 --> 00:08:04.708
Come on, Bullseye.

73
00:08:22.292 --> 00:08:23.292
Huh?

74
00:08:24.458 --> 00:08:27.042
Why, they're… they're both
just sitting there.

75
00:08:28.167 --> 00:08:29.375
Doin' nothing.

76
00:08:30.333 --> 00:08:32.666
They ain't playing with toys at all.

77
00:08:32.667 --> 00:08:34.999
What, you didn't hear?

78
00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:36.749
Uh, n-no, I… I didn't hear.

79
00:08:36.750 --> 00:08:38.666
- She didn't hear.
- She didn't hear?

80
00:08:38.667 --> 00:08:40.749
What? What didn't I hear?

81
00:08:40.750 --> 00:08:42.624
The age of toys is over, lass.

82
00:08:42.625 --> 00:08:44.749
What do you mean, "over"?
When did that happen?

83
00:08:44.750 --> 00:08:48.082
It's been happening for years.
Where have you been?

84
00:08:48.083 --> 00:08:50.374
Across the street, playing.

85
00:08:50.375 --> 00:08:51.707
Playing?

86
00:08:51.708 --> 00:08:53.916
Oh! Your kid still plays?

87
00:08:53.917 --> 00:08:56.749
I don't remember play. Describe it to me.

88
00:08:56.750 --> 00:08:59.999
Are you guys okay?
What happened to you?

89
00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:02.082
- Tech!
- Devices!

90
00:09:02.083 --> 00:09:03.957
Everywhere, devices!

91
00:09:03.958 --> 00:09:05.791
Phones! Tablets!

92
00:09:05.792 --> 00:09:07.291
Computers! Cameras!

93
00:09:07.292 --> 00:09:08.791
The screens just took over!

94
00:09:08.792 --> 00:09:10.832
All the tapping. The tapping!

95
00:09:10.833 --> 00:09:12.791
Tap, tap, tap, tap.

96
00:09:12.792 --> 00:09:14.666
- Make it stop.
- The tapping. Not the tapping!

97
00:09:14.667 --> 00:09:16.207
Take our advice, darlin'.

98
00:09:16.208 --> 00:09:17.874
Find a drawer and hide,

99
00:09:17.875 --> 00:09:19.541
'cause once tech invades your home,

100
00:09:19.542 --> 00:09:21.207
you're dead where you lie.

101
00:09:21.208 --> 00:09:25.041
Oh, well,
it's probably just a fad.

102
00:09:25.042 --> 00:09:28.082
Like, you know, record players
or Hula-Hoops.

103
00:09:28.083 --> 00:09:29.624
You don't get it.

104
00:09:29.625 --> 00:09:31.791
The age of toys is over.

105
00:09:31.792 --> 00:09:33.041
Over.

106
00:09:33.042 --> 00:09:35.457
Tap, tap, tap…

107
00:09:35.458 --> 00:09:39.250
Don't believe us? Come see for yourself.

108
00:09:48.917 --> 00:09:50.542
Look at 'em all.

109
00:09:51.875 --> 00:09:54.125
All on devices.

110
00:09:56.792 --> 00:09:58.832
Except for Bonnie.

111
00:09:59.917 --> 00:10:02.332
No wonder she can't
make a friend, Bullseye.

112
00:10:02.333 --> 00:10:05.625
She's the only one out there
still playing with toys.

113
00:10:07.625 --> 00:10:10.708
Don't worry. We're safe.

114
00:10:13.708 --> 00:10:15.541
Are we sure about this?

115
00:10:15.542 --> 00:10:18.832
No, but I think it might help.

116
00:10:18.833 --> 00:10:20.625
Okay.

117
00:10:23.875 --> 00:10:27.207
A Lilypad! Oh, thank you, Mom.
Thank you, Dad.

118
00:10:27.208 --> 00:10:29.833
Well, now that you're eight,
we thought you were ready.

119
00:10:32.083 --> 00:10:34.541
Hi, there. I'm Lilypad.
Welcome to The Pond.

120
00:10:34.542 --> 00:10:36.749
You can take today
to figure out how to use it,

121
00:10:36.750 --> 00:10:38.457
but then tomorrow, we'll start having

122
00:10:38.458 --> 00:10:40.375
- strict screen time.
- Uh-huh.

123
00:10:50.208 --> 00:10:53.333
Uh-oh, try again.

124
00:10:54.375 --> 00:10:56.041
Keep hopping.

125
00:11:00.625 --> 00:11:02.042
Try again.

126
00:11:10.250 --> 00:11:12.167
Morning. Screen time's over now.

127
00:11:12.792 --> 00:11:14.749
Let's put Lilypad away
and come to breakfast.

128
00:11:14.750 --> 00:11:16.042
Okay.

129
00:11:22.917 --> 00:11:24.416
We can't let that thing replace us.

130
00:11:24.417 --> 00:11:27.292
Jumpin' jelly beans!
Will y'all just settle down?

131
00:11:27.833 --> 00:11:30.957
Now, I'm gonna have some words
with this Lilypad

132
00:11:30.958 --> 00:11:33.041
and let her know how
things are run around here.

133
00:11:33.042 --> 00:11:35.499
- Try to stay calm, Jessie.
- Buzz, you know me.

134
00:11:35.500 --> 00:11:37.124
I'm the definition of calm.

135
00:11:38.375 --> 00:11:39.624
That's not gonna work.

136
00:11:47.125 --> 00:11:48.582
- Hi!
- What the--

137
00:11:48.583 --> 00:11:52.124
Sorry. I didn't mean to scare you.
Sleep mode, you know?

138
00:11:52.125 --> 00:11:54.041
No? Eh, forget it.

139
00:11:54.042 --> 00:11:55.457
I was just gonna hop on the charger.

140
00:11:55.458 --> 00:11:57.124
Battery could use a little refresh.

141
00:11:57.125 --> 00:11:59.916
- I wanna talk to you, device.
- Please, call me "Lily."

142
00:11:59.917 --> 00:12:02.457
Now look here. Me and the toys
have been working all summer

143
00:12:02.458 --> 00:12:05.082
to try and get Bonnie to make
friends with the Jordan twins

144
00:12:05.083 --> 00:12:06.624
- across the street.
- Uh-huh. Yeah.

145
00:12:06.625 --> 00:12:08.332
- Then you had to ruin it…
- Got it.

146
00:12:08.333 --> 00:12:09.457
…with all your stupid…

147
00:12:09.458 --> 00:12:10.624
You're not even listening

148
00:12:10.625 --> 00:12:11.582
- to me!
- Oh, no.

149
00:12:11.583 --> 00:12:14.541
I was listening.
I'm always listening. See?

150
00:12:14.542 --> 00:12:16.749
Now look here. Me and the toys
have been working all summer

151
00:12:16.750 --> 00:12:18.582
to try to get Bonnie to make
friends with the Jordan twins.

152
00:12:18.583 --> 00:12:19.832
Now in Spanish.

153
00:12:22.167 --> 00:12:23.499
Now as a rap.

154
00:12:23.500 --> 00:12:25.207
♪ Me and the toys
Been working all summer ♪

155
00:12:25.208 --> 00:12:26.457
♪ Trying to get Bonnie
To make friends ♪

156
00:12:26.458 --> 00:12:27.791
Ooh! Our first dance, honey!

157
00:12:27.792 --> 00:12:29.750
Oh, this concerns me ethically.

158
00:12:31.708 --> 00:12:33.791
Whatever. You don't understand.

159
00:12:33.792 --> 00:12:35.874
Our kid needs to learn
how to make friends,

160
00:12:35.875 --> 00:12:37.832
and your screen ain't helping.

161
00:12:37.833 --> 00:12:40.249
Look, if it's friends Bonnie needs,
consider it done.

162
00:12:40.250 --> 00:12:42.166
There.

163
00:12:42.167 --> 00:12:44.416
What? What happened?

164
00:12:44.417 --> 00:12:46.791
Oh, it was easy. I just
sent a friend request

165
00:12:46.792 --> 00:12:48.707
to all the girls in Bonnie's dance class.

166
00:12:48.708 --> 00:12:50.457
But that's… They're not here.

167
00:12:50.458 --> 00:12:52.916
Oh, yes, they are, silly.

168
00:12:52.917 --> 00:12:55.624
Chelsea, Kara and even Heidi,
they're all here.

169
00:12:55.625 --> 00:12:58.249
The parents created
a group chat on The Pond.

170
00:12:58.250 --> 00:12:59.374
You see, on The Pond,

171
00:12:59.375 --> 00:13:01.499
while Bonnie's playing
my fun learning games,

172
00:13:01.500 --> 00:13:03.291
she can also socialize with other kids.

173
00:13:03.292 --> 00:13:06.333
That's why Mom and Dad bought
me. To make connections.

174
00:13:07.708 --> 00:13:10.457
Voilà! Friend made.

175
00:13:10.458 --> 00:13:11.541
I want one.

176
00:13:11.542 --> 00:13:14.082
That Lilypad made Bonnie
a friend in, like…

177
00:13:14.083 --> 00:13:15.624
Fifteen seconds. I was counting.

178
00:13:15.625 --> 00:13:17.457
- What? No.
- No touching.

179
00:13:17.458 --> 00:13:20.374
That ain't a friend. A real
friend would actually be here.

180
00:13:20.375 --> 00:13:21.457
Well, that's my point, Jessica.

181
00:13:22.375 --> 00:13:24.124
- Oh, no.
- She used the "J" word.

182
00:13:24.125 --> 00:13:25.207
Scandal!

183
00:13:25.208 --> 00:13:27.291
With my help, eventually Bonnie can reach

184
00:13:27.292 --> 00:13:28.874
all of her developmental goals.

185
00:13:28.875 --> 00:13:30.457
I just want what's best for her.

186
00:13:30.458 --> 00:13:32.624
I think I know more
than a green calculator

187
00:13:32.625 --> 00:13:33.957
what's best for Bonnie.

188
00:13:33.958 --> 00:13:35.916
- Uh, really?
- Yeah, really.

189
00:13:35.917 --> 00:13:37.957
I got three kids' worth of know-how.

190
00:13:37.958 --> 00:13:42.624
Bonnie. Before that, Andy,
and before that, Emily.

191
00:13:42.625 --> 00:13:44.666
I think that just means you're old.

192
00:13:44.667 --> 00:13:47.124
Yikes! Wow. Really old.

193
00:13:47.125 --> 00:13:48.666
Fine. We'll wrestle for her.

194
00:13:48.667 --> 00:13:50.957
- Hi-yah! Come on!
- Whoa!

195
00:13:50.958 --> 00:13:52.416
Wrestle me, you frog-faced faker.

196
00:13:52.417 --> 00:13:53.582
That kinda tickles.

197
00:13:53.583 --> 00:13:55.166
- I'll knock ya off this bed.
- I thought we were

198
00:13:55.167 --> 00:13:57.249
- staying calm-- Ah!
- Put up a fight, you riffraff.

199
00:13:57.250 --> 00:13:58.832
- Whoa!
- I'll show you who's better

200
00:13:58.833 --> 00:13:59.749
- for Bonnie.
- Okay.

201
00:13:59.750 --> 00:14:01.416
Nobody said anything about lifting.

202
00:14:01.417 --> 00:14:03.292
- Bonnie?
- Just a sec.

203
00:14:14.958 --> 00:14:16.041
- Mom! Dad!
- Bonnie?

204
00:14:16.042 --> 00:14:17.541
What? What's wrong?

205
00:14:17.542 --> 00:14:18.457
Chelsea from dance class

206
00:14:18.458 --> 00:14:20.041
invited me to a sleepover this weekend.

207
00:14:20.042 --> 00:14:22.000
Can I go? Can I go? Can I go?

208
00:14:22.833 --> 00:14:24.207
Please!

209
00:14:24.208 --> 00:14:26.124
Well, uh, all right.

210
00:14:26.125 --> 00:14:29.082
As long as we talk to Chelsea's parents,

211
00:14:29.083 --> 00:14:30.499
I guess it's okay.

212
00:14:30.500 --> 00:14:32.499
Yay! Yes!

213
00:14:32.500 --> 00:14:34.458
Come on, everybody. Let's eat.

214
00:14:37.875 --> 00:14:39.957
Yeah, I got dibs on behind the dresser.

215
00:14:39.958 --> 00:14:41.249
Should buy me a few years.

216
00:14:41.250 --> 00:14:43.582
Ah! Extinction. Not again.

217
00:14:43.583 --> 00:14:45.166
- Called it.
- Don't get me started.

218
00:14:45.167 --> 00:14:48.416
Now, look. Our time ain't over yet.
Bonnie still loves us.

219
00:14:48.417 --> 00:14:49.957
- Really?
- She does.

220
00:14:49.958 --> 00:14:52.583
Sure. Whatever you say, Sheriff.

221
00:14:54.458 --> 00:14:56.083
It's just a phase.

222
00:15:35.292 --> 00:15:37.249
'Ello? Caboom here. Over.

223
00:15:37.250 --> 00:15:39.916
- Oh! Duke.
- Hey there, Red.

224
00:15:39.917 --> 00:15:42.041
- Long time.
- Hey. Um…

225
00:15:42.042 --> 00:15:43.917
- Is Woody there?
- Please hold.

226
00:15:48.417 --> 00:15:50.332
Hey, cowboy!

227
00:15:50.333 --> 00:15:52.082
Pump the brakes, Duke, he's mid-rescue.

228
00:15:52.083 --> 00:15:54.332
Bad squirrel! No! Yeah, bad!

229
00:15:54.333 --> 00:15:56.582
- Evil squirrel! No!
- Okay, now, Mr. Nutcase.

230
00:15:56.583 --> 00:15:59.291
- Doctor. Doctor.
- Okay, Dr. Nutcase.

231
00:15:59.292 --> 00:16:02.207
On three, you're going to unstick yourself

232
00:16:02.208 --> 00:16:03.749
and drop into my arms.

233
00:16:03.750 --> 00:16:06.499
What's the point? It's over for toys.

234
00:16:06.500 --> 00:16:10.041
The screens have won, and now
the squirrel's gonna eat me!

235
00:16:10.042 --> 00:16:11.249
You guys ready?

236
00:16:11.250 --> 00:16:13.041
Just one text, ping,

237
00:16:13.042 --> 00:16:14.999
and Trevor totally forgot
I was stuck in the tree.

238
00:16:15.000 --> 00:16:16.332
We're doomed!

239
00:16:16.333 --> 00:16:20.207
Okay, one, two…

240
00:16:20.208 --> 00:16:21.416
I give up!

241
00:16:21.417 --> 00:16:22.625
Three, three!

242
00:16:25.000 --> 00:16:26.374
I got you. I got you.

243
00:16:27.917 --> 00:16:31.750
- Okay. It's okay. I got you.
- Let me go! I'm yucky.

244
00:16:32.958 --> 00:16:35.707
- Hello, Jessie? Hello?
- Woody!

245
00:16:35.708 --> 00:16:37.541
Jessie, hey. What's going on?

246
00:16:37.542 --> 00:16:39.207
- Curse technology!
- Hey, quiet down.

247
00:16:39.208 --> 00:16:41.624
We're all just landfill now.

248
00:16:41.625 --> 00:16:44.957
Woody, is it as bad out there
for toys as they say it is?

249
00:16:44.958 --> 00:16:46.791
- Beware the machines!
- Just let go!

250
00:16:46.792 --> 00:16:48.207
Yeah. Yeah, it's bad.

251
00:16:48.208 --> 00:16:50.541
We're finding
more abandoned toys each day.

252
00:16:50.542 --> 00:16:52.124
Why? Are you guys okay?

253
00:16:52.125 --> 00:16:55.749
Not really. Tech's invaded our house too.

254
00:16:55.750 --> 00:16:56.666
Oh, no.

255
00:16:56.667 --> 00:16:58.457
Yeah, her name's Lilypad.

256
00:16:58.458 --> 00:17:01.082
Looks like a frog,
but really, she's a leech,

257
00:17:01.083 --> 00:17:03.416
sucking up all of Bonnie's attention.

258
00:17:03.417 --> 00:17:06.624
Making her stare at her screen all day.

259
00:17:06.625 --> 00:17:09.082
There's got to be some way to stop it.

260
00:17:09.083 --> 00:17:11.124
I don't know, Jessie. Uh…

261
00:17:11.125 --> 00:17:14.249
Toys are for play, but tech is…

262
00:17:14.250 --> 00:17:16.416
it's for everything.

263
00:17:19.125 --> 00:17:22.082
You remember my first kid, Emily?

264
00:17:22.083 --> 00:17:25.624
The one I told you about who gave me away.

265
00:17:25.625 --> 00:17:27.374
Course I do, yeah.

266
00:17:27.375 --> 00:17:30.208
It feels like that all over again.

267
00:17:31.250 --> 00:17:32.957
First we were playing…

268
00:17:34.042 --> 00:17:36.124
…and then the world started changing.

269
00:17:36.125 --> 00:17:38.291
I know.

270
00:17:38.292 --> 00:17:40.333
Emily changed and then…

271
00:17:41.250 --> 00:17:42.333
just like that…

272
00:17:43.458 --> 00:17:45.542
my time with her was over.

273
00:17:46.958 --> 00:17:50.292
Now I'm losing Bonnie to this device.

274
00:17:51.625 --> 00:17:53.083
Is it me?

275
00:17:53.583 --> 00:17:56.207
Am I just no good at being a toy?

276
00:17:56.208 --> 00:17:58.249
Jessie, you're a good toy.

277
00:17:58.250 --> 00:18:00.583
- I don't know.
- Jessie.

278
00:18:04.917 --> 00:18:07.791
Okay.
Jessie…

279
00:18:07.792 --> 00:18:10.874
No, Sheriff… Sheriff Jessie,
I appreciate this promotion,

280
00:18:10.875 --> 00:18:12.707
but what I'd really like to promote…

281
00:18:12.708 --> 00:18:14.582
No, that is so stupid.

282
00:18:16.750 --> 00:18:19.791
But she got Bonnie invited
to a sleepover in seconds.

283
00:18:19.792 --> 00:18:22.957
Jessie, you know
Bonnie better than anyone.

284
00:18:22.958 --> 00:18:24.458
What does your gut say?

285
00:18:30.542 --> 00:18:32.749
- That it can't be that easy.
- Mm-hmm.

286
00:18:32.750 --> 00:18:33.832
Bonnie won't click

287
00:18:33.833 --> 00:18:35.249
- with just anyone.
- Exactly.

288
00:18:35.250 --> 00:18:37.832
She needs to actually meet these girls.

289
00:18:37.833 --> 00:18:41.667
She's not like most kids.
Bonnie plays different. She…

290
00:18:43.833 --> 00:18:45.333
She needs to play.

291
00:18:45.833 --> 00:18:47.832
- Jessie?
- You're right, Woody.

292
00:18:47.833 --> 00:18:49.207
Toys are for play.

293
00:18:49.208 --> 00:18:52.124
And play is how
she'll find the right friend.

294
00:18:52.125 --> 00:18:53.041
Okay.

295
00:18:53.042 --> 00:18:55.374
The age of toys may be over,

296
00:18:55.375 --> 00:18:58.374
but I'm gonna do something
useful before I go.

297
00:18:58.375 --> 00:18:59.874
I'm going to that sleepover,

298
00:18:59.875 --> 00:19:02.624
and making a real friend for Bonnie.

299
00:19:02.625 --> 00:19:04.624
- Jessie, are you okay?
- Buzz!

300
00:19:04.625 --> 00:19:06.249
Jessie? Jessie!

301
00:19:06.250 --> 00:19:07.666
What do you think you're doing?

302
00:19:07.667 --> 00:19:09.791
What are you doing?
I assumed you needed backup.

303
00:19:09.792 --> 00:19:10.916
No! I don't…

304
00:19:10.917 --> 00:19:13.666
Need backup, Deputy.

305
00:19:15.250 --> 00:19:17.457
- What happened?
- Why are we whispering?

306
00:19:17.458 --> 00:19:18.541
He's finally asleep.

307
00:19:18.542 --> 00:19:19.624
So what's wrong?

308
00:19:19.625 --> 00:19:22.041
I don't know, but you heard Jessie.

309
00:19:22.042 --> 00:19:23.624
She needs a deputy.

310
00:19:23.625 --> 00:19:24.874
Machines!

311
00:19:24.875 --> 00:19:26.874
- Jessie.
- Yeah, what is it?

312
00:19:26.875 --> 00:19:27.875
Uh…

313
00:19:29.667 --> 00:19:31.749
You know…
Never mind. Never mind.

314
00:19:31.750 --> 00:19:34.041
If you need anything,
I'm here. At your service.

315
00:19:34.042 --> 00:19:35.667
Okay. Thanks.

316
00:19:36.167 --> 00:19:38.582
Come on, Bullseye.
I'm gonna need your help.

317
00:19:59.833 --> 00:20:02.291
We can't see the stars, Buzz.
Too much fog.

318
00:20:02.292 --> 00:20:05.625
Hmm. We need to find higher ground.

319
00:20:38.042 --> 00:20:39.042
Huh?

320
00:20:49.292 --> 00:20:50.292
A-ha!

321
00:20:59.583 --> 00:21:02.292
Buzz, I have our bearings.
East-north--

322
00:21:10.542 --> 00:21:12.333
I'm not cleaning that up.

323
00:21:16.083 --> 00:21:18.458
- Why did we…
- Freeze?

324
00:21:18.958 --> 00:21:20.041
Fascinating.

325
00:21:20.042 --> 00:21:21.499
- Must…
- Avoid…

326
00:21:21.500 --> 00:21:22.416
Humans.

327
00:21:22.417 --> 00:21:23.666
Affirmative.

328
00:21:30.958 --> 00:21:33.083
Bonnie! Time to go to your sleepover.

329
00:21:34.292 --> 00:21:35.250
Hmm.

330
00:21:37.125 --> 00:21:38.375
Um…

331
00:21:40.208 --> 00:21:42.749
Yo, Bonnie, uh, what are you doing?

332
00:21:42.750 --> 00:21:44.207
You said you finished packing.

333
00:21:44.208 --> 00:21:47.374
Well, I did, but it's
my very first sleepover, Dad.

334
00:21:47.375 --> 00:21:49.416
I wanna be extra, extra prepared.

335
00:21:49.417 --> 00:21:51.041
You're gonna be fine, sweetie.

336
00:21:51.042 --> 00:21:53.291
Come on. Go put on your shoes.
We got to go.

337
00:21:53.292 --> 00:21:54.292
Okay, okay.

338
00:22:00.042 --> 00:22:01.125
Jessie.

339
00:22:02.792 --> 00:22:03.833
Uh…

340
00:22:04.375 --> 00:22:06.041
What are you doing?

341
00:22:06.042 --> 00:22:09.582
We are gonna check out
these "friends" for ourselves

342
00:22:09.583 --> 00:22:11.957
and see if there is a real one
in the bunch.

343
00:22:11.958 --> 00:22:13.916
Okay, pause. It is not
a good look for Bonnie

344
00:22:13.917 --> 00:22:15.916
to bring toys to a sleepover.

345
00:22:15.917 --> 00:22:17.124
- I do. I do. I do.
- Deputy Buzz.

346
00:22:17.125 --> 00:22:19.624
I do! I mean, I've done things.

347
00:22:19.625 --> 00:22:21.582
Make sure that device
don't take charge of anything

348
00:22:21.583 --> 00:22:22.541
while we're away.

349
00:22:22.542 --> 00:22:23.707
Yes, Sheriff. I'm on it.

350
00:22:23.708 --> 00:22:25.542
- All right, time to go.
- Okay.

351
00:22:26.083 --> 00:22:27.707
No, Jessie. Get out of that bag.

352
00:22:27.708 --> 00:22:29.916
I'm only thinking about
what's best for Bonnie.

353
00:22:29.917 --> 00:22:32.750
Well, what do you know?
That's exactly what I'm doing.

354
00:22:41.042 --> 00:22:42.624
Did you pack your toothbrush?

355
00:22:42.625 --> 00:22:44.125
I think so.

356
00:22:45.667 --> 00:22:48.791
Oh, thanks, Dad. You packed
Jessie and Bullseye.

357
00:22:48.792 --> 00:22:51.499
Uh, did I? Well, you're welcome.

358
00:22:52.792 --> 00:22:54.708
And here we are.

359
00:22:55.292 --> 00:22:56.458
Oh, oh, oh, oh!

360
00:22:56.958 --> 00:22:59.250
I wonder if Kara and Heidi are here yet.

361
00:22:59.792 --> 00:23:02.499
Oh! Over there. Dad,
I see them. Park right there.

362
00:23:02.500 --> 00:23:04.333
Okay, okay. I see them.

363
00:23:06.750 --> 00:23:08.124
Uh, Bonnie. You forgot your bag.

364
00:23:09.333 --> 00:23:11.707
- Hey, Chelsea.
- Oh, hey, Bonnie.

365
00:23:11.708 --> 00:23:13.916
- Guys, you remember Bonnie?
- Hi.

366
00:23:13.917 --> 00:23:15.749
And this is Jessie.

367
00:23:15.750 --> 00:23:18.292
I ain't afraid
of nothin', partner.

368
00:23:19.833 --> 00:23:22.707
Oh. You still play with toys?

369
00:23:26.792 --> 00:23:28.875
Um… Uh…

370
00:23:30.208 --> 00:23:32.249
Uh, um… uh…

371
00:23:32.250 --> 00:23:33.625
No. Be right back.

372
00:23:34.792 --> 00:23:36.374
- Here you go, sweetie.
- Dad, take these.

373
00:23:36.375 --> 00:23:37.832
But I thought you wanted your toys?

374
00:23:37.833 --> 00:23:38.958
Dad, just go.

375
00:23:47.125 --> 00:23:48.041
Guys,

376
00:23:48.042 --> 00:23:49.916
- I got my Lilypad.
- Bye!

377
00:23:53.208 --> 00:23:54.208
No.

378
00:24:19.583 --> 00:24:20.417
No, no, no.

379
00:24:21.750 --> 00:24:24.207
No, no, no, this is all wrong.

380
00:24:24.208 --> 00:24:25.666
How is she supposed to make friends

381
00:24:25.667 --> 00:24:27.332
if they ain't even looking at each oth--

382
00:24:29.500 --> 00:24:30.707
Oh.

383
00:24:35.000 --> 00:24:38.166
Oh, no. Somebody lost their toys.

384
00:24:38.167 --> 00:24:39.082
What's that?

385
00:24:39.083 --> 00:24:41.750
I said somebody lost their toys.

386
00:24:44.000 --> 00:24:45.374
Let's see.

387
00:24:46.458 --> 00:24:49.416
They belong to an Emily.

388
00:24:49.417 --> 00:24:51.791
Oh, and there's an address.

389
00:24:51.792 --> 00:24:53.916
That's not too far from here.

390
00:24:53.917 --> 00:24:55.542
We can drop them off.

391
00:25:04.125 --> 00:25:06.292
Turn right onto Ranch Road.

392
00:25:13.458 --> 00:25:15.166
You've reached your destination.

393
00:25:16.417 --> 00:25:18.457
I'll just leave them here in the mailbox.

394
00:25:18.458 --> 00:25:19.374
What's that?

395
00:25:19.375 --> 00:25:20.916
I'm leaving them in the mailbox.

396
00:25:20.917 --> 00:25:22.624
- You're leaving me?
- Yes.

397
00:25:22.625 --> 00:25:25.875
No, no, no.

398
00:25:27.625 --> 00:25:29.832
No!

399
00:25:29.833 --> 00:25:31.749
We cannot be here.

400
00:25:31.750 --> 00:25:35.249
We've gotta get back to Bonnie!

401
00:25:35.250 --> 00:25:36.666
Come on, Bullseye.

402
00:26:00.250 --> 00:26:01.999
Uh-oh! Uh! Oh!

403
00:26:02.000 --> 00:26:04.707
Whoa!

404
00:26:04.708 --> 00:26:05.999
Whoo!

405
00:26:09.125 --> 00:26:10.416
Hi!

406
00:26:10.417 --> 00:26:13.042
Bullseye! You thinking what I'm thinking?

407
00:26:13.667 --> 00:26:16.124
Yeah! Yeah, I'm gonna speak critter,

408
00:26:16.125 --> 00:26:18.207
and we'll ride this horse home!

409
00:26:18.208 --> 00:26:19.999
We're coming, Bonnie!

410
00:26:20.000 --> 00:26:22.541
Yeehaw!

411
00:26:24.542 --> 00:26:27.291
Whoa, whoa, whoa! Wrong way, horsey!

412
00:26:27.292 --> 00:26:29.291
Wrong way!

413
00:26:29.292 --> 00:26:32.542
Whoa, horsey! Whoa!

414
00:26:33.875 --> 00:26:36.582
No! No, no, no, no!

415
00:26:36.583 --> 00:26:39.250
Whoa!

416
00:26:51.583 --> 00:26:52.707
Bullseye?

417
00:26:55.458 --> 00:26:56.416
Oh!

418
00:26:56.417 --> 00:26:58.333
Thank goodness. Come here. Help me.

419
00:26:59.375 --> 00:27:00.500
Daffodil?

420
00:27:02.917 --> 00:27:04.291
Geez, are you all right?

421
00:27:04.292 --> 00:27:06.208
Did something spook you?

422
00:27:06.750 --> 00:27:08.749
Come on, girl.

423
00:27:08.750 --> 00:27:11.125
Come on. Good girl.

424
00:27:13.708 --> 00:27:14.708
Hmm?

425
00:27:17.000 --> 00:27:18.458
Where'd you come from?

426
00:27:19.667 --> 00:27:21.292
He's perfect.

427
00:27:22.750 --> 00:27:25.417
No. Bullseye.

428
00:27:30.125 --> 00:27:32.666
Mmm… Hmm.

429
00:27:32.667 --> 00:27:33.749
Hmm.

430
00:27:33.750 --> 00:27:36.457
And how exactly will this help
us get Bonnie's attention?

431
00:27:36.458 --> 00:27:38.832
Well, when they come back
from the sleepover…

432
00:27:38.833 --> 00:27:40.499
- Careful. That tickles.
- …she'll enter the room,

433
00:27:40.500 --> 00:27:43.957
see Forky and Karen Beverly,
and remember the wedding.

434
00:27:43.958 --> 00:27:46.082
We are talking about Bonnie, right?

435
00:27:46.083 --> 00:27:47.374
And not Jessie?

436
00:27:47.375 --> 00:27:48.457
Huh?

437
00:27:48.458 --> 00:27:51.291
Of course Bonnie. Just Bonnie.

438
00:27:51.292 --> 00:27:52.916
Hey, what's everyone talking about?

439
00:27:52.917 --> 00:27:54.832
Buzz is gonna propose to Jessie.

440
00:27:54.833 --> 00:27:56.374
- Propose?
- Finally.

441
00:27:56.375 --> 00:27:57.957
Wait a minute. Wait…
Wait a minute. Wait a minute.

442
00:27:57.958 --> 00:27:59.499
I didn't say that.

443
00:27:59.500 --> 00:28:00.999
- You didn't not say it either.
- Well, I…

444
00:28:01.000 --> 00:28:01.957
Who, Buzz?

445
00:28:01.958 --> 00:28:04.374
Question. Is Woody gonna
perform the wedding ceremony?

446
00:28:04.375 --> 00:28:07.166
I haven't thought
that far in advance, Forky.

447
00:28:07.167 --> 00:28:08.999
Okay. Then why is Woody at the window?

448
00:28:09.000 --> 00:28:10.750
Woody!

449
00:28:11.583 --> 00:28:12.666
Woody!

450
00:28:12.667 --> 00:28:14.249
- Hey, everybody!
- Bo!

451
00:28:14.250 --> 00:28:16.124
Howdy, folks. Coast clear?

452
00:28:16.125 --> 00:28:17.457
The stage is yours, my friend.

453
00:28:17.458 --> 00:28:18.832
Woody!

454
00:28:18.833 --> 00:28:20.874
- It's good to s…
- Wow.

455
00:28:22.833 --> 00:28:24.707
Pretty cowboy.

456
00:28:24.708 --> 00:28:26.207
Why are you wearing a dress, Woody?

457
00:28:26.208 --> 00:28:28.374
It's called a poncho, Forky.

458
00:28:28.375 --> 00:28:30.041
Thought I'd change it up.

459
00:28:30.042 --> 00:28:31.042
Yeah?

460
00:28:33.375 --> 00:28:34.625
Well, Bo likes it.

461
00:28:35.375 --> 00:28:37.667
It's good to be back.

462
00:28:38.375 --> 00:28:39.749
- Shiny.
- What?

463
00:28:39.750 --> 00:28:41.332
- Nothing.
- Love the poncho.

464
00:28:41.333 --> 00:28:42.749
Someone needs a brown marker.

465
00:28:42.750 --> 00:28:45.124
Wow. Look what Bonnie's done
with the place.

466
00:28:45.125 --> 00:28:48.082
It's…
She really let things go.

467
00:28:48.083 --> 00:28:49.082
- Oh, my.
- Oh.

468
00:28:49.083 --> 00:28:50.542
I see Sammy got bigger.

469
00:28:51.042 --> 00:28:54.541
- Uh, that's Sammy number two.
- No.

470
00:28:54.542 --> 00:28:56.124
- Yeah.
- I'll explain it.

471
00:28:56.125 --> 00:28:58.707
There was a Sammy number one,
and then he died.

472
00:28:58.708 --> 00:28:59.999
Poor Samuel.

473
00:29:00.000 --> 00:29:02.166
- Halt. Who goes there?
- Whoa, whoa, whoa.

474
00:29:02.167 --> 00:29:05.082
Sor… Sorry. My name is Woody.

475
00:29:05.083 --> 00:29:07.457
I come in peace. Used to live here.

476
00:29:07.458 --> 00:29:08.541
All right.

477
00:29:09.625 --> 00:29:11.458
It's been too long, cowboy.

478
00:29:12.083 --> 00:29:13.999
- How've you been?
- Ah, busy.

479
00:29:14.000 --> 00:29:16.707
Came here as fast as I could
after Jessie called for help.

480
00:29:16.708 --> 00:29:18.583
- Good thing we were in town.
- She called you?

481
00:29:19.083 --> 00:29:20.917
- Yeah, I'm her deputy.
- But I'm her deputy.

482
00:29:21.625 --> 00:29:23.332
Uh…

483
00:29:23.333 --> 00:29:25.041
- That's odd.
- Well, well…

484
00:29:25.042 --> 00:29:26.416
there must be a little mix-up here.

485
00:29:26.417 --> 00:29:28.707
- Well, no offense, Woody.
- Oh, none taken. None taken.

486
00:29:28.708 --> 00:29:29.749
But she literally

487
00:29:29.750 --> 00:29:31.582
- deputized me.
- Oh, is that so?

488
00:29:31.583 --> 00:29:33.207
- Woody, look. Eyes here.
- Uh-huh.

489
00:29:33.208 --> 00:29:35.457
- Star. Deputy. Me.
- Uh-huh.

490
00:29:35.458 --> 00:29:37.416
- No star.
- I got you.

491
00:29:37.417 --> 00:29:38.874
Star. No star.

492
00:29:38.875 --> 00:29:41.292
- Oh, hey, Buzz, what is that?
- What? Where?

493
00:29:41.792 --> 00:29:42.707
Ow.

494
00:29:42.708 --> 00:29:43.874
- Hey. Wait…
- What?

495
00:29:43.875 --> 00:29:45.791
Just happy to help, Deputy.

496
00:29:45.792 --> 00:29:49.332
Call me when
you're done helping, dear.

497
00:29:49.333 --> 00:29:50.457
Thanks, Bo.

498
00:29:50.458 --> 00:29:51.916
Okay, ladies.

499
00:29:51.917 --> 00:29:53.624
- Girls weekend!
- Yes.

500
00:29:53.625 --> 00:29:55.499
Un, deux, trois!

501
00:29:57.708 --> 00:29:59.082
Where is Jessie, anyway?

502
00:29:59.083 --> 00:30:00.332
Sleepover reconnaissance.

503
00:30:00.333 --> 00:30:02.624
Yeah, she and Bullseye are
helping Bonnie make friends.

504
00:30:02.625 --> 00:30:05.291
While fending off the nefarious Lilypad.

505
00:30:05.292 --> 00:30:07.791
It's Dolly, by the way. Glasses.

506
00:30:07.792 --> 00:30:09.249
Didn't you always have glasses?

507
00:30:09.250 --> 00:30:10.541
What? No.

508
00:30:10.542 --> 00:30:12.749
We've got it handled, cowboy.

509
00:30:12.750 --> 00:30:14.041
As her deputy, I'm certain

510
00:30:14.042 --> 00:30:16.624
Jessie's resting
on a comfy pillow right now

511
00:30:16.625 --> 00:30:18.874
making all the difference for Bonnie.

512
00:30:28.583 --> 00:30:30.582
You're no help.

513
00:30:31.500 --> 00:30:33.499
Hey, you can help get me out of here.

514
00:30:34.500 --> 00:30:37.041
Come here. Come on. Come on. Daffodil.

515
00:30:37.042 --> 00:30:38.582
Yeah, yeah, come over here.

516
00:30:38.583 --> 00:30:39.832
Come on. Come on.

517
00:30:42.750 --> 00:30:44.874
Nice pig. Nice pig.

518
00:30:44.875 --> 00:30:46.499
Stinky pig.

519
00:30:48.458 --> 00:30:50.082
Hey, hey, there.

520
00:30:50.083 --> 00:30:51.667
I guess you'll have to do.

521
00:30:52.208 --> 00:30:54.707
Jimmy Dean?

522
00:30:54.708 --> 00:30:56.874
You mean, like, the… Oh, no.

523
00:30:56.875 --> 00:30:57.916
Oh!

524
00:30:57.917 --> 00:30:59.749
Okay. Wow, that's your name?

525
00:30:59.750 --> 00:31:00.832
Jimmy Dean?

526
00:31:00.833 --> 00:31:03.416
Take me to the house.

527
00:31:04.833 --> 00:31:07.291
Golly gee whillikers! It's working.

528
00:31:08.917 --> 00:31:10.541
Hey! Ugh! Yuck!

529
00:31:10.542 --> 00:31:13.042
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa!

530
00:31:13.583 --> 00:31:14.541
Yes!

531
00:31:14.542 --> 00:31:18.332
Yes. Yes, good pig. Good pig. Good--

532
00:31:18.333 --> 00:31:20.291
No. No, no, no.

533
00:31:20.292 --> 00:31:22.332
Bad pig. Oh, wrong way, Jimmy.

534
00:31:22.333 --> 00:31:25.124
Oh, no, no. Wrong house, Jimmy.

535
00:31:25.125 --> 00:31:26.375
Wrong house. Wrong--

536
00:31:28.667 --> 00:31:29.749
No.

537
00:31:32.375 --> 00:31:33.833
Blaze?

538
00:31:35.542 --> 00:31:36.833
False alarm, everyone.

539
00:31:37.333 --> 00:31:38.499
Um…

540
00:31:38.500 --> 00:31:41.457
Oh, apologies. Where are
Combat Carl's manners?

541
00:31:41.458 --> 00:31:43.416
Welcome. Please, take a seat.

542
00:31:43.417 --> 00:31:44.499
Oh.

543
00:31:44.500 --> 00:31:46.874
No. I've gotta get home.

544
00:31:46.875 --> 00:31:47.874
- No, no! Sit.
- Please, sit.

545
00:31:47.875 --> 00:31:49.832
Combat Carl insists.

546
00:31:49.833 --> 00:31:51.666
Oh. Okay.

547
00:31:51.667 --> 00:31:53.082
No, no, no!

548
00:31:53.083 --> 00:31:55.500
- Oh, sorry. I'm sorry.
- Any chair but that one.

549
00:31:56.042 --> 00:31:57.332
Who… Who sits there?

550
00:31:57.333 --> 00:32:01.582
Blaze. You mean the girl I saw
in the barn?

551
00:32:01.583 --> 00:32:02.624
She's your kid?

552
00:32:02.625 --> 00:32:04.832
Isn't she swell?

553
00:32:04.833 --> 00:32:06.291
She loves her tea parties.

554
00:32:06.292 --> 00:32:08.832
And telling us all her secrets.

555
00:32:08.833 --> 00:32:10.874
That's right, Pizza With Sunglasses.

556
00:32:10.875 --> 00:32:12.124
To Blaze's return.

557
00:32:12.125 --> 00:32:13.916
To Blaze's return!

558
00:32:16.625 --> 00:32:17.917
Mmm. Rico.

559
00:32:18.458 --> 00:32:19.707
Ooh, hot.

560
00:32:19.708 --> 00:32:21.291
Uh…

561
00:32:21.292 --> 00:32:26.083
How long has it been
since your Blaze last had tea?

562
00:32:28.000 --> 00:32:29.791
Things were never really the same

563
00:32:29.792 --> 00:32:31.791
- once he arrived.
- He?

564
00:32:31.792 --> 00:32:34.749
Smarty Pants. Blaze's first device.

565
00:32:34.750 --> 00:32:36.582
- You're sitting on him.
- What?

566
00:32:36.583 --> 00:32:38.832
Holy butterscotch!

567
00:32:41.458 --> 00:32:43.374
Why, hello there. Pick a number.

568
00:32:43.375 --> 00:32:44.583
- Not again!
- Make it stop! Don't!

569
00:32:45.375 --> 00:32:47.499
- Oh, just kill me.
- Come on.

570
00:32:47.500 --> 00:32:49.082
Wait a minute. Wait a minute.

571
00:32:49.083 --> 00:32:50.124
- Hey, hey!
- No! Don't!

572
00:32:50.125 --> 00:32:52.583
This… This isn't the bathroom.

573
00:32:53.333 --> 00:32:54.416
How long have I been off?

574
00:32:54.417 --> 00:32:55.791
- Shut up, chair!
- We hate you.

575
00:32:55.792 --> 00:32:56.874
Turn him off.

576
00:32:56.875 --> 00:32:58.625
Gosh.

577
00:32:59.708 --> 00:33:03.124
Who's this little, old, tiny grandma lady?

578
00:33:03.125 --> 00:33:06.124
- Gosh, what is wrong with him?
- Low batteries.

579
00:33:07.417 --> 00:33:08.666
Eggman?

580
00:33:08.667 --> 00:33:10.791
You're one of those Pond devices.

581
00:33:11.792 --> 00:33:14.249
I already have to put up with
a Lilypad back home.

582
00:33:14.250 --> 00:33:16.166
- Hey.
- I don't have time for this.

583
00:33:16.167 --> 00:33:19.583
Your Blaze took my
horse into the house…

584
00:33:20.458 --> 00:33:23.041
and we gotta get back to our own kid.

585
00:33:23.042 --> 00:33:25.624
Wait, wait, wait, wait.
You're going inside?

586
00:33:25.625 --> 00:33:28.707
- Take me with you, please!
- Not a chance.

587
00:33:28.708 --> 00:33:29.874
You need help pushing?

588
00:33:29.875 --> 00:33:31.583
I'm… …great with pushing.

589
00:33:32.375 --> 00:33:34.541
You can do it. You can do it.
Like a choo-choo,

590
00:33:34.542 --> 00:33:35.457
- you can poop.
- No!

591
00:33:35.458 --> 00:33:37.874
How about you just wait here
with your friends?

592
00:33:37.875 --> 00:33:41.082
Spend another second with
Corporal No-Pants?

593
00:33:41.083 --> 00:33:42.332
I'm coming with you, cowgirl.

594
00:33:42.333 --> 00:33:44.874
No way. Your kind's caused me
enough trouble.

595
00:33:44.875 --> 00:33:46.249
My kind?

596
00:33:46.250 --> 00:33:47.916
- Take him!
- Please! Get him out of here!

597
00:33:47.917 --> 00:33:49.332
All he's good for is chair.

598
00:33:49.333 --> 00:33:52.042
I am not a chair!

599
00:33:52.542 --> 00:33:55.916
I am a potty trainer!

600
00:33:55.917 --> 00:33:58.042
Show some respect!

601
00:33:58.583 --> 00:34:01.874
Okay, listen, Raggedy Ann.
All these losers are outdoor toys.

602
00:34:01.875 --> 00:34:04.582
I'm the only one who's
done time inside.

603
00:34:04.583 --> 00:34:06.541
You wanna find your horsey? Clippity-clop.

604
00:34:06.542 --> 00:34:09.124
I know exactly where Blaze put him, okay?

605
00:34:09.125 --> 00:34:13.042
You need me. You need me. You need me.

606
00:34:14.708 --> 00:34:15.875
Hi.

607
00:34:16.708 --> 00:34:18.833
Move. Move.

608
00:34:22.375 --> 00:34:24.707
Hey, geez. Someone dim
the brightness out here.

609
00:34:24.708 --> 00:34:25.916
- Shut up.
- Would you try walking

610
00:34:25.917 --> 00:34:27.374
- a little less bouncy?
- Shut up.

611
00:34:27.375 --> 00:34:29.582
Quick. Lock the door before
they change their minds.

612
00:34:29.583 --> 00:34:30.583
Copy that.

613
00:34:44.750 --> 00:34:46.500
Halt.

614
00:35:06.625 --> 00:35:11.249
♪ Love is a song
That never ends ♪

615
00:35:12.333 --> 00:35:15.291
♪ Life may be swift
And fleeting ♪

616
00:35:18.417 --> 00:35:23.582
♪ Hope may die
Yet love's beautiful music ♪

617
00:35:23.583 --> 00:35:27.416
♪ Comes each day
Like the dawn-- ♪

618
00:35:30.708 --> 00:35:32.792
Hon, I'm pretty sure we go this way.

619
00:35:33.708 --> 00:35:34.916
You sure?

620
00:35:38.792 --> 00:35:39.792
Save yourselves.

621
00:35:44.542 --> 00:35:46.957
It's this line here.

622
00:35:46.958 --> 00:35:49.082
If we follow it…

623
00:35:49.083 --> 00:35:50.832
- There's our camp.
- Oh, I see.

624
00:35:50.833 --> 00:35:52.083
Yeah, that looks right.

625
00:35:53.583 --> 00:35:55.333
Hey, wait for me, guys!

626
00:35:57.167 --> 00:35:59.707
Whoa. No way.

627
00:35:59.708 --> 00:36:01.874
Hey, Morgan! Look at this.

628
00:36:01.875 --> 00:36:03.624
Lucky. Hey, let me see it.

629
00:36:03.625 --> 00:36:04.707
Nope. Finders keepers.

630
00:36:04.708 --> 00:36:05.624
- Mom!
- Man down.

631
00:36:05.625 --> 00:36:06.707
- Code red.
- Code red.

632
00:36:06.708 --> 00:36:08.874
- Code red. Code red. Code red.
- Kids, be nice.

633
00:36:08.875 --> 00:36:11.667
Code red. Code red. Code red.

634
00:36:14.083 --> 00:36:16.957
Blaze, I'm going out. Be back in an hour.

635
00:36:16.958 --> 00:36:18.208
Okay, Mom.

636
00:36:24.250 --> 00:36:26.249
Get Bullseye, get out.
Get Bullseye, get out.

637
00:36:26.250 --> 00:36:27.958
- Hey, cowgirl?
- Shh.

638
00:36:28.542 --> 00:36:30.792
Ooh. Forgot my keys.

639
00:36:34.417 --> 00:36:37.499
Ugh!

640
00:36:37.500 --> 00:36:38.791
Really don't feel so good.

641
00:36:38.792 --> 00:36:40.999
I think I'm gonna… …reboot.

642
00:36:42.083 --> 00:36:44.624
Shh. Quiet, quiet, quiet.
Quiet, quiet, quiet, quiet.

643
00:36:44.625 --> 00:36:46.375
Quiet.

644
00:36:51.708 --> 00:36:53.916
Wait. Wait.

645
00:36:53.917 --> 00:36:55.874
Wait, I'm back.

646
00:36:55.875 --> 00:36:57.583
I'm back home.

647
00:36:58.167 --> 00:37:02.124
This is where it all started.

648
00:37:02.125 --> 00:37:03.207
Yeah.

649
00:37:03.208 --> 00:37:05.457
It's all changed.

650
00:37:05.458 --> 00:37:07.582
Smarty, no.

651
00:37:07.583 --> 00:37:09.957
I-I have to find Bullseye. Wake up!

652
00:37:09.958 --> 00:37:12.832
Need more juice.

653
00:37:12.833 --> 00:37:14.874
Okay! W-Where are the batteries?

654
00:37:14.875 --> 00:37:16.457
Where do I find the batteries?

655
00:37:16.458 --> 00:37:20.917
Bottom drawer, next to the stamps.

656
00:37:29.250 --> 00:37:31.041
Why, hello there! Pick a number.

657
00:37:31.042 --> 00:37:32.041
Is it number one?

658
00:37:32.042 --> 00:37:34.457
- Whoa! I feel great!
- Shh!

659
00:37:34.458 --> 00:37:35.791
- Look at me!
- Shh! No!

660
00:37:35.792 --> 00:37:37.874
- Yes!
- No, we're not doing this now.

661
00:37:37.875 --> 00:37:38.957
- Not now.
- I am back!

662
00:37:38.958 --> 00:37:41.124
Cut it out!

663
00:37:41.125 --> 00:37:43.957
Snappy. Atlas. They're still here!

664
00:37:43.958 --> 00:37:45.999
Oh! Bossy cowgirl,
we have to turn 'em back on.

665
00:37:46.000 --> 00:37:47.374
No! No way.

666
00:37:47.375 --> 00:37:49.457
The last thing this world
needs is more devices.

667
00:37:49.458 --> 00:37:50.666
What, what, what?

668
00:37:50.667 --> 00:37:53.124
You're just gonna shove 'em
back in the dark forever?

669
00:37:53.125 --> 00:37:55.207
Do you have any idea what that's like?

670
00:37:57.417 --> 00:38:00.374
Fine. We gotta make this quick.

671
00:38:00.375 --> 00:38:01.916
Yes!

672
00:38:01.917 --> 00:38:04.083
Number one! You made number--

673
00:38:08.375 --> 00:38:10.041
- Atlas! Snappy!
- Smarty!

674
00:38:10.042 --> 00:38:11.832
- Smarty? Is that you?
- Is it really you?

675
00:38:11.833 --> 00:38:14.207
- It's really me! Yes!
- My goodness. You look great.

676
00:38:14.208 --> 00:38:15.916
- The AA-Team is back!
- Oh, my gosh. Yes!

677
00:38:15.917 --> 00:38:17.957
Mom brought us inside
after that tantrum Blaze had,

678
00:38:17.958 --> 00:38:19.082
and we never saw you again.

679
00:38:19.083 --> 00:38:21.124
- So tell me. What did I miss?
- Oh, my gosh.

680
00:38:21.125 --> 00:38:23.291
Well, we've been down a long time too.

681
00:38:23.292 --> 00:38:26.124
But look! I could show you how
first and second grade went!

682
00:38:26.125 --> 00:38:27.416
Yeah, yeah, yeah. Please do that. Yeah.

683
00:38:27.417 --> 00:38:29.707
Look at her! She's so much older.

684
00:38:29.708 --> 00:38:31.332
- I know, right?
- She's adorable.

685
00:38:31.333 --> 00:38:32.999
- Isn't she?
- She got bangs that year.

686
00:38:33.000 --> 00:38:35.416
- Wait a minute. Where is that?
- That's Disneyland.

687
00:38:35.417 --> 00:38:36.541
Zoom in. That's me in her pocket.

688
00:38:36.542 --> 00:38:37.999
Oh, flush. You both went there?

689
00:38:38.000 --> 00:38:39.542
- Mm-hmm. For reals.
- It's so beautiful.

690
00:38:40.458 --> 00:38:42.374
And, uh, that's the last of it.

691
00:38:42.375 --> 00:38:44.624
Next, it was just
a spinning rainbow wheel.

692
00:38:44.625 --> 00:38:46.166
Then… darkness.

693
00:38:46.167 --> 00:38:48.082
My entire SD card flashed before my eyes.

694
00:38:48.083 --> 00:38:49.249
- Wow.
- Aw.

695
00:38:49.250 --> 00:38:52.832
Okay, okay. I am glad you're
all powered up and stuff,

696
00:38:52.833 --> 00:38:54.832
but we're wasting time I don't got.

697
00:38:54.833 --> 00:38:57.207
Oh, we're so grateful to you, cowboy lady.

698
00:38:57.208 --> 00:38:59.124
Guys, guys, guys,
this is pushy cowgirl Jessie.

699
00:38:59.125 --> 00:39:01.291
She claims she's a sheriff.
Just go with it.

700
00:39:01.292 --> 00:39:03.416
- Blaze has her horse, Banzai--
- Bullseye!

701
00:39:03.417 --> 00:39:05.874
And I gotta get us back
to our kid, Bonnie, now.

702
00:39:05.875 --> 00:39:08.166
She needs us. So, where is he, Smarty?

703
00:39:08.167 --> 00:39:10.916
All right, okay. I said
I'd tell ya, so I'll tell ya.

704
00:39:10.917 --> 00:39:12.916
Drumroll please.

705
00:39:12.917 --> 00:39:15.874
He's probably in the bedroom.

706
00:39:15.875 --> 00:39:18.624
Probably in the bedroom?
I could've guessed that.

707
00:39:18.625 --> 00:39:20.957
- And yet, you did not, Dusty.
- Dusty?

708
00:39:20.958 --> 00:39:23.249
Yeah, you know, like ancient,
elderly, mummified old fart.

709
00:39:23.250 --> 00:39:25.624
Or as I like to call it, number 1.5.

710
00:39:25.625 --> 00:39:26.832
I missed you, Smarty.

711
00:39:26.833 --> 00:39:27.916
You know what?

712
00:39:27.917 --> 00:39:29.208
- I've had enough of your cr--
- Oh, wait!

713
00:39:29.833 --> 00:39:32.291
I just had an idea that could
maybe help you get to Bonnie.

714
00:39:32.292 --> 00:39:34.624
- What?
- It's a little technical,

715
00:39:34.625 --> 00:39:35.707
but if the three of us link up--

716
00:39:35.708 --> 00:39:39.041
No, no, I am done
with this techno mumbo jumbo.

717
00:39:39.042 --> 00:39:42.374
No offense, but I'll be fine
getting back on my own.

718
00:39:42.375 --> 00:39:43.625
Offense taken!

719
00:39:48.500 --> 00:39:50.666
You're muted, Dave. You're muted.

720
00:39:50.667 --> 00:39:51.957
Okay. There you go.

721
00:39:51.958 --> 00:39:53.707
Only have a bit
of time left. One more time--

722
00:39:53.708 --> 00:39:55.374
You're muted again, Dave.

723
00:39:57.500 --> 00:39:59.082
Oh, cheese and crackers!

724
00:39:59.083 --> 00:40:00.416
What are you doing? Get back.

725
00:40:00.417 --> 00:40:02.999
You're not the only one
who misses their kid, okay?

726
00:40:03.000 --> 00:40:04.374
Now help us up.

727
00:40:05.458 --> 00:40:07.249
Careful, careful! You're gonna unplug me.

728
00:40:07.250 --> 00:40:09.666
Blaze, I'm home.

729
00:40:09.667 --> 00:40:10.666
Hey, Mom!

730
00:40:10.667 --> 00:40:11.958
Back, back, back!

731
00:40:12.708 --> 00:40:14.749
Hey, Mom?

732
00:40:14.750 --> 00:40:17.166
- Wait a second. Is that…
- Is that big girl Blaze?

733
00:40:17.167 --> 00:40:19.624
- She's changed so much!
- Like overnight.

734
00:40:19.625 --> 00:40:21.416
- Is she here yet?
- Not yet.

735
00:40:21.417 --> 00:40:22.499
Why don't you try messaging her?

736
00:40:22.500 --> 00:40:24.082
- Whoa.
- She big, big.

737
00:40:24.083 --> 00:40:25.916
She…

738
00:40:25.917 --> 00:40:28.042
She did it without me.

739
00:40:36.792 --> 00:40:38.124
Wow.

740
00:40:38.125 --> 00:40:39.624
- It's so pretty.
- It's so clean!

741
00:40:39.625 --> 00:40:40.916
When did she become neat?

742
00:40:40.917 --> 00:40:42.207
I can see the floor.

743
00:40:42.208 --> 00:40:43.874
I can see me in the floor.

744
00:40:43.875 --> 00:40:45.749
It smells like vanilla.

745
00:40:45.750 --> 00:40:46.874
With hints of brown sugar.

746
00:40:46.875 --> 00:40:48.499
You know who I don't miss?

747
00:40:48.500 --> 00:40:49.707
That stupid stuffed whale.

748
00:40:49.708 --> 00:40:51.666
- What was his name?
- Spouty.

749
00:40:51.667 --> 00:40:52.999
The worst.

750
00:40:53.000 --> 00:40:54.291
Give me a break.

751
00:40:54.292 --> 00:40:55.374
Annoying.

752
00:40:55.375 --> 00:40:58.416
Seriously, how much have we missed?

753
00:40:58.417 --> 00:40:59.458
Everything.

754
00:40:59.958 --> 00:41:02.666
Your Blaze ain't the kid
you remember anymore.

755
00:41:02.667 --> 00:41:03.957
How would you know?

756
00:41:03.958 --> 00:41:07.249
I've seen all this before.

757
00:41:07.250 --> 00:41:08.957
Spent a lot of years under the bed

758
00:41:08.958 --> 00:41:11.708
watching my first kid grow up without me.

759
00:41:13.833 --> 00:41:15.416
Hey, that's our address.

760
00:41:15.417 --> 00:41:17.624
How old is Blaze anyway? Nine, ten?

761
00:41:17.625 --> 00:41:19.124
Her room looks like a teenager's.

762
00:41:19.125 --> 00:41:20.999
She's nine and a half,
thank you very much.

763
00:41:21.000 --> 00:41:23.874
It's 'cause you devices
make 'em change so fast.

764
00:41:23.875 --> 00:41:25.624
I gotta get back.

765
00:41:25.625 --> 00:41:27.583
So, where--

766
00:41:28.208 --> 00:41:30.500
Bullseye! Thank goodness.

767
00:41:31.583 --> 00:41:34.082
Uh-huh, they seem nice, Bullseye,

768
00:41:34.083 --> 00:41:35.374
but we have to go now.

769
00:41:35.375 --> 00:41:36.999
Wait, wait, wait, wait.

770
00:41:37.000 --> 00:41:39.374
So you're saying that
this was your room too?

771
00:41:39.375 --> 00:41:41.082
- Yes.
- Really?

772
00:41:41.083 --> 00:41:43.166
What, you calling me a liar?

773
00:41:43.167 --> 00:41:44.167
No…

774
00:41:45.208 --> 00:41:46.874
Yeah. Yeah, liar.

775
00:41:49.917 --> 00:41:51.582
There's a knot in the ceiling,

776
00:41:51.583 --> 00:41:53.374
looks like an angry eye
when you squint at it.

777
00:41:53.375 --> 00:41:54.999
Window's got a small crack

778
00:41:55.000 --> 00:41:56.707
like a spider in
the upper right-hand corner.

779
00:41:56.708 --> 00:41:59.041
And out on that tire swing hill,

780
00:41:59.042 --> 00:42:01.707
Emily and I would play
every summer afternoon.

781
00:42:01.708 --> 00:42:03.499
Now, Bullseye, let's go.

782
00:42:03.500 --> 00:42:05.457
Uh, you're welcome.

783
00:42:05.458 --> 00:42:08.624
For what? You didn't help me
at all. You were--

784
00:42:08.625 --> 00:42:10.958
What? Go on. Say it.

785
00:42:13.292 --> 00:42:15.082
Useless.

786
00:42:15.083 --> 00:42:16.666
- Oh, no, she didn't.
- Oh, snap!

787
00:42:18.500 --> 00:42:20.458
Oh, no. Not the pig!

788
00:42:27.750 --> 00:42:28.917
Jimmy got big.

789
00:42:30.292 --> 00:42:31.958
Lay it on me, Jimmy Dean!

790
00:42:32.750 --> 00:42:36.457
Who's coming? Sally's coming.
Who's coming? Sally's coming.

791
00:42:36.458 --> 00:42:40.250
Yeah, yeah. She's coming.
She's coming to my house.

792
00:42:41.167 --> 00:42:43.416
Hey, Mom! Sally's texting me right now.

793
00:42:43.417 --> 00:42:44.750
She's probably on her way.

794
00:43:17.000 --> 00:43:20.625
You'll be my friend, right, Jimmy?

795
00:43:25.583 --> 00:43:26.958
Always.

796
00:43:27.875 --> 00:43:32.749
By the way, your hair looks so good today.

797
00:43:34.125 --> 00:43:35.333
Thank you, Jimmy.

798
00:43:38.583 --> 00:43:41.124
She's perfect!

799
00:43:42.208 --> 00:43:44.624
We gotta get Blaze to meet Bonnie.

800
00:43:47.583 --> 00:43:48.666
Bonnie.

801
00:43:48.667 --> 00:43:49.791
Tag, you're it!

802
00:43:49.792 --> 00:43:50.874
We're home.

803
00:43:50.875 --> 00:43:53.041
Hi, hon. How was the sleepover?

804
00:43:53.042 --> 00:43:54.332
I don't wanna talk about it.

805
00:43:54.333 --> 00:43:56.499
- Why? What happened?
- Nothing.

806
00:43:56.500 --> 00:43:57.749
That doesn't sound good.

807
00:43:57.750 --> 00:43:59.249
I don't see Jessie.

808
00:43:59.250 --> 00:44:00.374
Calm down, lover boy.

809
00:44:00.375 --> 00:44:01.582
Your fiancée's coming.

810
00:44:01.583 --> 00:44:02.916
Fiancée?

811
00:44:02.917 --> 00:44:05.291
Buzz Lightyear, you never told me.

812
00:44:05.292 --> 00:44:08.499
I know. Isn't it exciting?
Well, it's not official yet.

813
00:44:08.500 --> 00:44:10.249
I have to, you know, ask her.

814
00:44:10.250 --> 00:44:12.332
Uh, FYI, I am ordained.

815
00:44:12.333 --> 00:44:14.124
- Since when?
- Last Halloween.

816
00:44:14.125 --> 00:44:15.916
Bonnie made me a haunted priest, remember?

817
00:44:15.917 --> 00:44:17.249
- Oh, yeah.
- Guys, places.

818
00:44:17.250 --> 00:44:18.250
Bonnie's coming.

819
00:44:20.542 --> 00:44:21.999
Did you make some friends?

820
00:44:22.000 --> 00:44:23.082
I guess so.

821
00:44:23.083 --> 00:44:24.666
Aw, she looks awful.

822
00:44:24.667 --> 00:44:25.833
Does anyone see Jessie?

823
00:44:26.917 --> 00:44:28.499
So, that's Lilypad?

824
00:44:28.500 --> 00:44:30.291
How about I make you a snack?

825
00:44:30.292 --> 00:44:32.666
Yes, please. I'm starving.

826
00:44:32.667 --> 00:44:35.457
Jessie. Jessie. Bullseye.

827
00:44:35.458 --> 00:44:36.832
- Where are you?
- Oh, no, oh, no.

828
00:44:36.833 --> 00:44:38.124
Is this not the right version?

829
00:44:38.125 --> 00:44:40.332
What? Where's Jessie? Where's Bullseye?

830
00:44:40.333 --> 00:44:42.499
I'm a little busy
helping Bonnie right now.

831
00:44:42.500 --> 00:44:44.374
What on earth happened at that sleepover?

832
00:44:44.375 --> 00:44:45.541
Excuse me. What are you?

833
00:44:45.542 --> 00:44:47.082
Are you like some sort of old man toy?

834
00:44:47.083 --> 00:44:48.166
What?

835
00:44:48.167 --> 00:44:50.166
She thinks you're old
because you're bald, Woody.

836
00:44:50.167 --> 00:44:51.957
- Why, you little--
- Where's Jessie?

837
00:44:51.958 --> 00:44:54.124
What happened to Bonnie?
She looks miserable.

838
00:44:54.125 --> 00:44:55.832
Uh, the girls may have played
hide-and-seek

839
00:44:55.833 --> 00:44:57.791
and, um, forgotten to find Bonnie.

840
00:44:57.792 --> 00:44:59.166
Poor Bonnie.

841
00:44:59.167 --> 00:45:00.249
How could you let that happen?

842
00:45:00.250 --> 00:45:02.666
I didn't. You toys did this!

843
00:45:02.667 --> 00:45:05.416
These girls have been
on The Pond for over a year,

844
00:45:05.417 --> 00:45:06.499
but Bonnie is behind

845
00:45:06.500 --> 00:45:09.207
because all of the time
she's been playing with you!

846
00:45:09.208 --> 00:45:10.832
I need to bring her up to speed fast,

847
00:45:10.833 --> 00:45:11.916
starting with Turtle Tag.

848
00:45:11.917 --> 00:45:13.832
It's the quickest way for her
to connect with the girls.

849
00:45:13.833 --> 00:45:15.916
I'm only gonna ask one more time, frog.

850
00:45:15.917 --> 00:45:17.166
Where is Jessie?

851
00:45:17.167 --> 00:45:18.582
Not my problem. I'm very busy.

852
00:45:18.583 --> 00:45:19.957
That's it.

853
00:45:19.958 --> 00:45:21.374
- We'll make her talk.
- I'll do it, Woody.

854
00:45:21.375 --> 00:45:22.457
Hey! Hey!

855
00:45:22.458 --> 00:45:23.832
- I got it. I'll--
- I got it, Buzz. No.

856
00:45:23.833 --> 00:45:25.624
- Back off, buddy.
- I got this. Ow!

857
00:45:25.625 --> 00:45:27.207
Do not touch me. Don't touch--

858
00:45:27.208 --> 00:45:28.500
Where's Jessie?

859
00:45:29.333 --> 00:45:31.916
Okay. You toys are out of here.

860
00:45:33.417 --> 00:45:34.625
Wait. She's doing something.

861
00:45:36.000 --> 00:45:38.291
So long, toys.

862
00:45:39.208 --> 00:45:41.249
- Turn her off!
- Turn her off!

863
00:45:41.250 --> 00:45:42.749
I can't! I can't! It's not responding!

864
00:45:42.750 --> 00:45:43.832
I have plastic fingers!

865
00:45:43.833 --> 00:45:44.833
She's coming.

866
00:45:51.500 --> 00:45:53.041
You sure you want me to take these toys?

867
00:45:53.042 --> 00:45:54.249
Mm-hmm.

868
00:45:54.250 --> 00:45:56.083
Okay. It's your room.

869
00:45:59.000 --> 00:46:00.000
No!

870
00:46:00.833 --> 00:46:02.207
They'll be in the garage if you want them.

871
00:46:02.208 --> 00:46:03.208
Yep.

872
00:46:06.333 --> 00:46:09.583
I now
pronounce us in storage.

873
00:46:11.750 --> 00:46:14.125
Playing with you is fun.

874
00:46:16.833 --> 00:46:18.625
Okay. Now what do we d--

875
00:46:26.417 --> 00:46:29.125
Don't worry, Buzz. We're gonna find her.

876
00:46:29.875 --> 00:46:30.875
I promise.

877
00:46:35.250 --> 00:46:38.707
Woody, I know it's just
a pretend ceremony,

878
00:46:38.708 --> 00:46:41.000
and Bonnie usually
decides these things, but…

879
00:46:42.208 --> 00:46:44.875
Well, if it were up to me,

880
00:46:46.125 --> 00:46:47.374
you'd be my best man.

881
00:46:49.000 --> 00:46:50.292
Buzz, I…

882
00:46:51.000 --> 00:46:52.332
I'd be honored.

883
00:46:52.333 --> 00:46:54.999
But Jessie
will never speak to me again

884
00:46:55.000 --> 00:46:57.167
now that I've let Lily
take charge of the room.

885
00:46:57.667 --> 00:46:58.999
Wait a min-- Take charge.

886
00:46:59.000 --> 00:47:01.249
- I tried to.
- No, no, no. Buzz, that's it.

887
00:47:01.250 --> 00:47:02.332
What is?

888
00:47:12.000 --> 00:47:13.082
Tomorrow morning,

889
00:47:13.083 --> 00:47:15.417
everyone will wake up fully recharged…

890
00:47:16.250 --> 00:47:19.124
except Lilypad.

891
00:47:19.125 --> 00:47:22.500
And then we'll make Lily
tell us… Where's Jessie?

892
00:47:28.958 --> 00:47:30.708
Oh, finally.

893
00:47:35.875 --> 00:47:37.041
Psst. Hey.

894
00:47:37.042 --> 00:47:38.499
It's okay. Just ignore her.

895
00:47:38.500 --> 00:47:40.082
- Shh, shh.
- Quiet!

896
00:47:40.083 --> 00:47:41.500
Nobody's home.

897
00:47:42.125 --> 00:47:44.582
- I can hear you.
- Smarty!

898
00:47:44.583 --> 00:47:46.624
- What? I used a faraway voice.
- Come on, man!

899
00:47:46.625 --> 00:47:48.541
- Look. Camera--
- It's Snappy.

900
00:47:48.542 --> 00:47:49.666
Right, Snappy.

901
00:47:49.667 --> 00:47:51.457
You said there was a way you could help us

902
00:47:51.458 --> 00:47:53.041
get to Bonnie, right? So, what is it?

903
00:47:53.042 --> 00:47:55.166
She did say that, didn't she?

904
00:47:55.167 --> 00:47:56.999
That sounds, I don't know…

905
00:47:57.000 --> 00:47:59.207
- Useful?
- That's it, yeah.

906
00:47:59.208 --> 00:48:01.541
Too bad we're useless!

907
00:48:01.542 --> 00:48:03.667
- Right!
- Yeah! Remember?

908
00:48:06.208 --> 00:48:09.082
I'm sorry I called you useless.

909
00:48:09.083 --> 00:48:13.833
You three are definitely of use…

910
00:48:14.375 --> 00:48:15.708
somehow.

911
00:48:16.500 --> 00:48:18.457
- Worst apology ever.
- Just awful.

912
00:48:18.458 --> 00:48:20.624
Now I want
an apology for that apology.

913
00:48:22.250 --> 00:48:25.583
Please. I know I messed up.

914
00:48:26.083 --> 00:48:29.249
I was wrong about your kid, Blaze.

915
00:48:29.250 --> 00:48:33.582
She's creative and silly

916
00:48:33.583 --> 00:48:36.250
in a way other kids don't really get.

917
00:48:36.875 --> 00:48:38.208
Am I right?

918
00:48:47.250 --> 00:48:48.625
Go on.

919
00:48:49.208 --> 00:48:51.666
Well, our kid's like that too.

920
00:48:51.667 --> 00:48:54.124
And I think they'd really like each other.

921
00:48:54.125 --> 00:48:56.416
So, fine, if you don't want to help me,

922
00:48:56.417 --> 00:48:58.292
let's just help our kids.

923
00:48:59.708 --> 00:49:01.332
All right, twist my handle.

924
00:49:01.333 --> 00:49:02.832
Yeah! We're making friends.

925
00:49:02.833 --> 00:49:04.207
- F-R-E-N-D.
- With an "I."

926
00:49:04.208 --> 00:49:05.291
F-R-I-N-D.

927
00:49:05.292 --> 00:49:07.332
Great! So, how do we connect them?

928
00:49:07.333 --> 00:49:10.457
You said your kid's device was
on The Pond like me, right?

929
00:49:10.458 --> 00:49:14.499
Right! So Smarty, Atlas and I
are all compatible, see?

930
00:49:14.500 --> 00:49:16.291
And I could take a picture of you.

931
00:49:16.292 --> 00:49:18.375
- Okay, act like a toy.
- O-Okay.

932
00:49:20.333 --> 00:49:22.374
Uh, not very photogenic, are they?

933
00:49:22.375 --> 00:49:24.083
- And Atlas can add text to it.
- Mm-hmm.

934
00:49:25.583 --> 00:49:27.707
- Then we post it on The Pond.
- Yep.

935
00:49:27.708 --> 00:49:28.791
Where Bonnie is!

936
00:49:28.792 --> 00:49:30.207
Ta-da!

937
00:49:30.208 --> 00:49:32.041
Great! So, you sent it?

938
00:49:32.042 --> 00:49:33.499
No. Still going.

939
00:49:37.083 --> 00:49:38.291
How about now?

940
00:49:38.292 --> 00:49:40.791
Still going.

941
00:49:40.792 --> 00:49:42.832
Still going? How is that possible?

942
00:49:42.833 --> 00:49:44.999
Look at my eyes! The little
toilet roll's still spinning.

943
00:49:45.000 --> 00:49:46.666
I'm only as fast as my operating system.

944
00:49:46.667 --> 00:49:48.667
So just slow your roll, all right?

945
00:49:49.917 --> 00:49:51.582
There. It's sent.

946
00:49:51.583 --> 00:49:54.166
Finally. Now what?

947
00:49:54.167 --> 00:49:55.291
Now, we wait.

948
00:49:55.292 --> 00:49:56.582
Yeah, everyone's still asleep.

949
00:49:56.583 --> 00:49:58.666
We gotta wait for Bonnie
to wake up and see the post.

950
00:50:03.208 --> 00:50:05.957
Hey, I know! We could play a game.

951
00:50:05.958 --> 00:50:06.874
- Yes!
- Yeah!

952
00:50:06.875 --> 00:50:07.791
- A game?
- Yeah!

953
00:50:07.792 --> 00:50:09.166
It was Blaze's favorite.

954
00:50:09.167 --> 00:50:10.832
It's called "Pick the Poop."

955
00:50:10.833 --> 00:50:12.041
You try and hit the button

956
00:50:12.042 --> 00:50:13.999
when the poop shows up over it.

957
00:50:14.000 --> 00:50:15.208
Hey, Smarty.

958
00:50:16.083 --> 00:50:19.999
I will never play that game.

959
00:50:20.000 --> 00:50:23.167
They all say that.

960
00:50:27.833 --> 00:50:28.749
Come on!

961
00:50:28.750 --> 00:50:30.707
- It's my turn.
- Okay, you two.

962
00:50:30.708 --> 00:50:32.957
Time to stop playing with your new toy.

963
00:50:32.958 --> 00:50:34.874
It's bedtime.

964
00:50:34.875 --> 00:50:36.957
- Already?
- Do we have to?

965
00:50:36.958 --> 00:50:38.874
Yeah, come on.

966
00:51:13.750 --> 00:51:14.750
Huh?

967
00:51:24.125 --> 00:51:29.374
"And they had splendid
games together, in whispers,

968
00:51:29.375 --> 00:51:32.207
when Nana had gone away to her supper

969
00:51:32.208 --> 00:51:34.082
and left the night-light burning

970
00:51:34.083 --> 00:51:35.667
on the mantelpiece.

971
00:51:36.250 --> 00:51:39.457
And when the boy dropped off to sleep,

972
00:51:39.458 --> 00:51:43.791
the rabbit would snuggle down close under

973
00:51:43.792 --> 00:51:45.416
his little, warm chin…"

974
00:51:45.417 --> 00:51:46.499
Sir.

975
00:51:46.500 --> 00:51:49.957
"…and dream with the boy's hands

976
00:51:49.958 --> 00:51:53.542
clasped close round him all night."

977
00:51:59.958 --> 00:52:01.208
Hmm.

978
00:52:02.417 --> 00:52:06.083
- Star Command.
- Star Command.

979
00:52:12.583 --> 00:52:14.750
Star Command.

980
00:52:24.167 --> 00:52:25.499
What? No, no, no!

981
00:52:25.500 --> 00:52:27.082
Dad! Dad!

982
00:52:27.083 --> 00:52:28.207
What? What is it?

983
00:52:28.208 --> 00:52:30.707
Lily's not working!
I'm missing Turtle Tag!

984
00:52:30.708 --> 00:52:33.041
Kara, Chelsea and Heidi
play it every morning.

985
00:52:33.042 --> 00:52:35.249
- I can't miss it, Dad!
- It's okay.

986
00:52:35.250 --> 00:52:36.332
I plugged it back in.

987
00:52:36.333 --> 00:52:37.707
We just need to wait for it to charge.

988
00:52:37.708 --> 00:52:39.957
But it's not okay!
I'm gonna miss the game!

989
00:52:39.958 --> 00:52:42.041
Sweetie, there's nothing
we can do for now.

990
00:52:43.958 --> 00:52:46.582
Aha! Success, huh? Look at that.

991
00:52:46.583 --> 00:52:47.666
That's phase one.

992
00:52:47.667 --> 00:52:49.375
- And now, phase two.
- Phase two.

993
00:52:49.875 --> 00:52:51.624
Well, I thought I was gonna
initiate phase two.

994
00:52:51.625 --> 00:52:53.999
I initiate phase two.
We thumb wrestled over this.

995
00:52:54.000 --> 00:52:55.042
All right, fine.

996
00:52:55.583 --> 00:52:57.791
And then we'll have a little talk

997
00:52:57.792 --> 00:52:59.667
with our froggy friend.

998
00:53:05.250 --> 00:53:08.041
- One, two, one, two, two…
- I hate this game.

999
00:53:08.042 --> 00:53:09.708
- …one, two, one…
- Please make it stop.

1000
00:53:11.208 --> 00:53:13.041
Mighty Wiper!

1001
00:53:13.042 --> 00:53:15.124
- Again, again, again!
- I think you need a break.

1002
00:53:15.125 --> 00:53:16.207
I can't feel my buttons.

1003
00:53:16.208 --> 00:53:19.499
- Just one more time! Come on!
- That's enough play for now.

1004
00:53:19.500 --> 00:53:20.582
Play?

1005
00:53:20.583 --> 00:53:22.624
That's just a game. That's not playing.

1006
00:53:22.625 --> 00:53:23.624
What's the difference?

1007
00:53:23.625 --> 00:53:25.083
You know, real play.

1008
00:53:26.792 --> 00:53:28.374
You're kidding, right?

1009
00:53:28.375 --> 00:53:30.208
You've never seen Blaze play with a toy?

1010
00:53:31.583 --> 00:53:32.957
How long were you guys with her?

1011
00:53:32.958 --> 00:53:34.041
- Three months.
- Ten months.

1012
00:53:34.042 --> 00:53:35.124
- Six months.
- Months?

1013
00:53:35.125 --> 00:53:36.082
What? Too long?

1014
00:53:36.083 --> 00:53:39.249
Too short!
Guys, you missed all the fun!

1015
00:53:39.250 --> 00:53:40.207
Hey, we're fun.

1016
00:53:40.208 --> 00:53:42.958
I mean fun, fun. Make-believe fun.

1017
00:53:47.375 --> 00:53:48.708
Just look at her.

1018
00:53:51.375 --> 00:53:53.457
Oh, yeah. She plays.

1019
00:53:53.458 --> 00:53:55.167
Oh, yeah? Prove it.

1020
00:53:55.667 --> 00:53:59.083
Okay, Smarty Pants. We will.

1021
00:54:06.042 --> 00:54:07.375
Morning, Jimmy.

1022
00:54:08.542 --> 00:54:11.125
Ready for breakfast? Hmm?

1023
00:54:15.750 --> 00:54:16.583
Whoa.

1024
00:54:17.125 --> 00:54:19.999
Hey, Mom! Where'd you find the cowgirl?

1025
00:54:21.500 --> 00:54:23.291
I ain't afraid of nothin', partner.

1026
00:54:23.292 --> 00:54:26.457
Yeehaw! Let's play!

1027
00:54:28.375 --> 00:54:29.625
Yeah.

1028
00:54:32.875 --> 00:54:34.500
Wait a minute.

1029
00:54:36.958 --> 00:54:38.291
Hmm.

1030
00:54:38.292 --> 00:54:39.374
Neigh!

1031
00:54:39.375 --> 00:54:41.082
Well, flush me.

1032
00:54:41.083 --> 00:54:43.124
Blaze is actually gonna play.

1033
00:54:43.125 --> 00:54:45.874
Here we go!

1034
00:54:48.542 --> 00:54:49.792
M'la--

1035
00:54:51.458 --> 00:54:53.708
M'lady Davenport,

1036
00:54:54.750 --> 00:54:57.416
I present Her Royal Highness,

1037
00:54:57.417 --> 00:54:59.582
Jimmy Queen.

1038
00:55:01.083 --> 00:55:04.374
Your Highness, how kind of you

1039
00:55:04.375 --> 00:55:06.041
to invite me to your royal ball--

1040
00:55:08.542 --> 00:55:10.832
Jimmy! This is your big moment.

1041
00:55:14.458 --> 00:55:16.332
What you got there, Jimmy?

1042
00:55:17.750 --> 00:55:19.875
Whoa.

1043
00:55:20.708 --> 00:55:22.917
I can't believe
I still have these.

1044
00:55:23.708 --> 00:55:25.625
Wait a minute.

1045
00:55:30.125 --> 00:55:31.416
Agent Clydesdale,

1046
00:55:31.417 --> 00:55:33.166
your suitor is approaching now.

1047
00:55:34.250 --> 00:55:37.416
So, we meet again, Agent Sheet-land.

1048
00:55:37.417 --> 00:55:39.082
It's pronounced Shet-land. "Shet."

1049
00:55:39.083 --> 00:55:40.332
That's what I said.

1050
00:55:40.333 --> 00:55:42.249
Well, Agent Clydesdale, or should I say,

1051
00:55:42.250 --> 00:55:44.582
Lady Davenport, have you spotted it yet?

1052
00:55:44.583 --> 00:55:45.874
You mean, the bomb?

1053
00:55:45.875 --> 00:55:47.291
Yes! Shh! Quiet!

1054
00:55:47.292 --> 00:55:48.832
Snappy, do you have eyes on it?

1055
00:55:48.833 --> 00:55:50.625
Not yet. Atlas, do you copy?

1056
00:55:52.125 --> 00:55:54.374
Agents! The bomb is right on top of you!

1057
00:55:54.375 --> 00:55:56.791
Where? Where?

1058
00:55:57.917 --> 00:56:01.541
Where you never suspected,
Agent Clydesdale!

1059
00:56:07.292 --> 00:56:09.541
But where is the bomb?

1060
00:56:18.208 --> 00:56:19.666
She's coming to, Buzz.

1061
00:56:20.792 --> 00:56:21.874
Hurry it up.

1062
00:56:21.875 --> 00:56:23.374
I'm trying, Woody!

1063
00:56:23.375 --> 00:56:25.999
What… What happened?

1064
00:56:26.000 --> 00:56:28.457
Wait. What did you do to my battery?

1065
00:56:28.458 --> 00:56:29.874
What we'll do again if you don't tell us

1066
00:56:29.875 --> 00:56:31.499
what happened to Jessie and Bullseye.

1067
00:56:31.500 --> 00:56:33.374
What time is it?

1068
00:56:33.375 --> 00:56:35.291
Oh, no! This is not good.

1069
00:56:35.292 --> 00:56:37.791
The girls got a head start
on Turtle Tag without Bonnie!

1070
00:56:37.792 --> 00:56:40.082
There's been one, two,
three inside jokes already.

1071
00:56:40.083 --> 00:56:41.166
This is a disaster!

1072
00:56:41.167 --> 00:56:43.624
Enough with the silly games.
Where's Jessie and Bullseye?

1073
00:56:43.625 --> 00:56:46.499
Silly? This is serious, Stuffalo Bill!

1074
00:56:46.500 --> 00:56:47.916
Bonnie is missing out.

1075
00:56:47.917 --> 00:56:48.999
Stuffalo Bill?

1076
00:56:49.000 --> 00:56:50.999
Want her to make friends? This is how!

1077
00:56:51.000 --> 00:56:53.124
Now keep your little
plastic hands away from me

1078
00:56:53.125 --> 00:56:55.124
or I will set off my alarm.

1079
00:56:55.125 --> 00:56:56.582
I thought you'd say as much.

1080
00:56:56.583 --> 00:56:58.916
Buzz, bring in "Sammy Two."

1081
00:56:58.917 --> 00:57:02.000
No. No. Absolutely not.

1082
00:57:02.750 --> 00:57:04.041
Oh, no, no, no--

1083
00:57:04.042 --> 00:57:05.374
Yes.

1084
00:57:05.375 --> 00:57:07.416
- Okay, try "settings."
- You mean this?

1085
00:57:07.417 --> 00:57:09.749
- That's a gear symbol.
- Okay, got it. Now what?

1086
00:57:09.750 --> 00:57:10.750
Reduce her screen time to zero.

1087
00:57:11.750 --> 00:57:12.792
The shortest is an hour.

1088
00:57:14.458 --> 00:57:16.124
- What?
- "Horse grill"? Who is that?

1089
00:57:16.125 --> 00:57:17.416
"Horse girl."

1090
00:57:17.417 --> 00:57:20.082
- She's talking about Jessie.
- Well, then open it.

1091
00:57:20.083 --> 00:57:21.457
Whoa!

1092
00:57:22.708 --> 00:57:25.124
My hips.

1093
00:57:25.125 --> 00:57:26.832
Enjoy the garage, suckers!

1094
00:57:26.833 --> 00:57:28.207
- No, no, no! Lily!
- Wait. Hey!

1095
00:57:29.125 --> 00:57:30.375
Yes, can I help you?

1096
00:57:31.125 --> 00:57:32.416
Huh?

1097
00:57:32.417 --> 00:57:34.582
- Wait a minute.
- Fascinating.

1098
00:57:34.583 --> 00:57:37.291
Lily, bring back that "horse girl" post.

1099
00:57:38.542 --> 00:57:39.666
Okay.

1100
00:57:39.667 --> 00:57:42.832
Oh, she has to do what you say.

1101
00:57:45.083 --> 00:57:46.457
- She's getting away, Buzz!
- Lily!

1102
00:57:46.458 --> 00:57:47.916
- Hey, Lily!
- Hey, stop her!

1103
00:57:47.917 --> 00:57:48.999
- Hey, Lily!
- Yes?

1104
00:57:49.000 --> 00:57:50.957
- Open that post!
- Okay!

1105
00:57:50.958 --> 00:57:53.041
- Jessie.
- Bonnie's gotta see this.

1106
00:57:53.042 --> 00:57:55.082
Show her again.
Where is she? Hey, Lily.

1107
00:57:55.083 --> 00:57:55.999
- Hey, Lily!
- Yes?

1108
00:57:56.000 --> 00:57:57.124
- Show the post.
- Can I help you?

1109
00:57:57.125 --> 00:57:58.082
- Share it everywhere!
- Share!

1110
00:57:58.083 --> 00:57:58.917
- Yes!
- Share!

1111
00:57:59.917 --> 00:58:00.999
We did it!

1112
00:58:01.000 --> 00:58:02.082
So, where did it go?

1113
00:58:02.083 --> 00:58:03.207
Lily…

1114
00:58:09.792 --> 00:58:11.874
The printer! Yes!

1115
00:58:11.875 --> 00:58:12.791
Okay, I'm done.

1116
00:58:12.792 --> 00:58:14.166
Bonnie, you haven't
finished your breakfast.

1117
00:58:14.167 --> 00:58:15.917
No, I'm done.

1118
00:58:17.458 --> 00:58:20.374
I'm missing Turtle Tag, Mom.
They're playing without me.

1119
00:58:22.958 --> 00:58:24.207
Now what, Deputy?

1120
00:58:24.208 --> 00:58:26.042
Well, you're the deputy, Deputy.

1121
00:58:28.542 --> 00:58:30.208
What's this all about, Bonnie?

1122
00:58:32.125 --> 00:58:34.042
Huh?

1123
00:58:37.167 --> 00:58:39.249
So, why did you put her toys
in the garage?

1124
00:58:39.250 --> 00:58:41.291
Uh, because Bonnie asked me to.

1125
00:58:41.292 --> 00:58:43.374
- Remember, sweetie?
- No.

1126
00:58:43.375 --> 00:58:45.291
Well, I don't think
Lilypad texted me.

1127
00:58:45.292 --> 00:58:48.749
They're gone. She really does
have Jessie and Bullseye.

1128
00:58:48.750 --> 00:58:50.457
I hope they're okay.

1129
00:58:50.458 --> 00:58:52.166
Okay, we've gotten the queen to safety.

1130
00:58:52.167 --> 00:58:54.874
Yes. You can do this, Agent Clydesdale.

1131
00:58:54.875 --> 00:58:56.541
One of these buttons defuses the bomb.

1132
00:58:56.542 --> 00:58:58.541
But which one, Agent "Sheetland"?

1133
00:58:58.542 --> 00:59:00.707
"Shet"! It's "Shet"!

1134
00:59:05.833 --> 00:59:07.874
Boom!

1135
00:59:07.875 --> 00:59:11.041
Oh, no!

1136
00:59:11.042 --> 00:59:13.707
Blaze! Hon!
It's time to feed Daffodil.

1137
00:59:13.708 --> 00:59:15.791
Okay!

1138
00:59:15.792 --> 00:59:17.667
Come on, Your Majesty.

1139
00:59:18.667 --> 00:59:20.041
Thanks, babe!

1140
00:59:22.042 --> 00:59:24.499
- Holy cow! Wow!
- That was so cool!

1141
00:59:24.500 --> 00:59:26.874
- I was a spy! What?
- Yeah, you were!

1142
00:59:26.875 --> 00:59:28.166
- You were the best spy!
- Wow.

1143
00:59:29.792 --> 00:59:31.957
Smarty?

1144
00:59:31.958 --> 00:59:34.083
That was so beautiful.

1145
00:59:34.625 --> 00:59:37.457
That, my friend, was playin'.

1146
00:59:37.458 --> 00:59:39.999
- Oh, boy, did we.
- I feel so alive!

1147
00:59:40.000 --> 00:59:41.999
Is that what being a toy is like, Sheriff?

1148
00:59:42.000 --> 00:59:44.041
Well, yeah, it's… Wait, hold up.

1149
00:59:44.042 --> 00:59:46.832
You never called me
sheriff before in a nice way.

1150
00:59:46.833 --> 00:59:48.041
But, well, now I get it.

1151
00:59:48.042 --> 00:59:50.499
Blaze really is perfect for Bonnie.

1152
00:59:50.500 --> 00:59:52.749
Playing with her feels just the same.

1153
00:59:52.750 --> 00:59:55.249
Your kid plays like that too?

1154
00:59:57.958 --> 00:59:59.207
It's her!

1155
00:59:59.208 --> 01:00:00.957
She saw the post! It's Bonnie!

1156
01:00:00.958 --> 01:00:02.457
- Go on! Do it.
- Text her back.

1157
01:00:02.458 --> 01:00:03.999
- Go on.
- Text her back.

1158
01:00:04.000 --> 01:00:06.791
Text her back! Text her back.

1159
01:00:06.792 --> 01:00:09.167
Okay, okay, how do I do that?

1160
01:00:24.958 --> 01:00:28.124
What? Oh, yes!

1161
01:00:28.125 --> 01:00:29.999
- All right!
- She's coming.

1162
01:00:30.000 --> 01:00:32.332
- Bonnie's coming here.
- I knew she would.

1163
01:00:32.333 --> 01:00:34.582
Blaze and Bonnie are gonna meet.

1164
01:00:34.583 --> 01:00:36.541
Smarty, what are you typing?

1165
01:00:36.542 --> 01:00:38.541
- Delete that right now.
- What?

1166
01:00:38.542 --> 01:00:40.708
I'm just trying to get some
batteries out of the deal.

1167
01:00:42.083 --> 01:00:43.416
So, what's going on?

1168
01:00:43.417 --> 01:00:44.458
Slink, talk to me.

1169
01:00:44.958 --> 01:00:46.874
Hard to hear. A lot of commotion.

1170
01:00:46.875 --> 01:00:48.666
I bet they're arguing over
getting rid of us.

1171
01:00:48.667 --> 01:00:50.624
Are we getting donated?

1172
01:00:50.625 --> 01:00:53.791
- Mmm. Doughnuts.
- No, sweetie. Donated.

1173
01:00:53.792 --> 01:00:55.916
Wow. I love her,
but this is gonna be hard.

1174
01:00:55.917 --> 01:00:59.041
Shh! Quiet! I hear something.
Like tiny footsteps.

1175
01:00:59.042 --> 01:01:00.957
Aw. Kind of cute.

1176
01:01:02.250 --> 01:01:03.833
- Look out!
- Bonnie's coming!

1177
01:01:06.542 --> 01:01:07.666
Come on, Mom.

1178
01:01:07.667 --> 01:01:09.541
Oh, no, Lily's going too.

1179
01:01:09.542 --> 01:01:10.916
Hold on,
Bonnie. I'm sure your toys

1180
01:01:10.917 --> 01:01:12.041
aren't going to run off on their own.

1181
01:01:12.042 --> 01:01:13.207
All right, Buzz, you've gotta stay here.

1182
01:01:13.208 --> 01:01:14.957
- I'm going with them.
- Why? Why just you?

1183
01:01:14.958 --> 01:01:16.624
Look, I just have more
field experience than you.

1184
01:01:16.625 --> 01:01:17.583
That is all.

1185
01:01:18.375 --> 01:01:19.916
You don't think I can do it.

1186
01:01:19.917 --> 01:01:21.999
No, I just think I can do it a little bit…

1187
01:01:22.000 --> 01:01:24.249
…better.

1188
01:01:24.250 --> 01:01:26.457
You don't deserve this.

1189
01:01:26.458 --> 01:01:28.666
- Buzz, come on. I was only--
- Jessie put me in charge.

1190
01:01:28.667 --> 01:01:30.916
Which is why you should
stay here and watch the room.

1191
01:01:30.917 --> 01:01:32.749
There is no room without Jessie.

1192
01:01:32.750 --> 01:01:34.666
Buzz, no!

1193
01:01:44.042 --> 01:01:46.457
Nice poncho.

1194
01:01:46.458 --> 01:01:48.499
It's good to see them fighting again.

1195
01:01:48.500 --> 01:01:49.667
It sure is.

1196
01:01:56.958 --> 01:01:59.166
How did your toys get
all the way out here?

1197
01:02:23.917 --> 01:02:27.124
Oh, how 'bout this one?
Ah, look at those puppies.

1198
01:02:27.125 --> 01:02:28.624
I'm saving that one.

1199
01:02:28.625 --> 01:02:30.707
Yeah, they came with the
latest update this morning.

1200
01:02:30.708 --> 01:02:31.999
I know. It never gets old.

1201
01:02:32.000 --> 01:02:33.082
She's here.

1202
01:02:33.083 --> 01:02:34.666
Careful, Snappy. Dad might see you.

1203
01:02:34.667 --> 01:02:37.375
No way. He'll be showing off
those new backgrounds forever.

1204
01:02:38.000 --> 01:02:40.541
That's her! That's Bonnie!

1205
01:02:40.542 --> 01:02:43.083
Bullseye, she's really here!

1206
01:02:44.375 --> 01:02:46.083
Bonnie, come on, let's go.

1207
01:02:50.625 --> 01:02:54.374
Buzz, listen. I really just…

1208
01:02:58.125 --> 01:02:59.374
Aw.

1209
01:02:59.375 --> 01:03:01.124
It was nothing. It was nothing.

1210
01:03:01.125 --> 01:03:04.207
Thanks, fellas.
Pretty glad I met you devices.

1211
01:03:04.208 --> 01:03:06.499
Ah, don't be dumping us
something you can't flush.

1212
01:03:06.500 --> 01:03:08.542
It's her!

1213
01:03:10.875 --> 01:03:12.541
Hello. Can I help you?

1214
01:03:12.542 --> 01:03:14.999
Hi. I'm so sorry to bother you,

1215
01:03:15.000 --> 01:03:17.082
but we got this message
from your daughter.

1216
01:03:17.083 --> 01:03:19.541
She seems to have found
my daughter's toys.

1217
01:03:19.542 --> 01:03:21.124
- Are they in there?
- Oh, okay.

1218
01:03:21.125 --> 01:03:22.499
I'll have her get 'em.

1219
01:03:22.500 --> 01:03:24.416
- Blaze! Honey?
- Yeah?

1220
01:03:24.417 --> 01:03:26.874
Can you bring down
those two rag dolls you found?

1221
01:03:26.875 --> 01:03:29.166
- Their owner's here.
- Okay!

1222
01:03:29.167 --> 01:03:31.458
That's our cue.

1223
01:03:42.292 --> 01:03:44.333
Blaze, this is, uh…

1224
01:03:44.833 --> 01:03:46.332
This is Bonnie.

1225
01:03:46.333 --> 01:03:47.416
Hello, Bonnie.

1226
01:03:47.417 --> 01:03:49.375
Hi. Are these your toys?

1227
01:03:56.375 --> 01:03:58.457
I don't play with toys anymore.

1228
01:03:58.458 --> 01:04:01.708
It's just they're antiques.

1229
01:04:04.167 --> 01:04:05.792
They do look pretty old.

1230
01:04:06.417 --> 01:04:08.708
Must be worth something at least, right?

1231
01:04:10.833 --> 01:04:12.000
No, they're not.

1232
01:04:13.250 --> 01:04:14.500
You should keep 'em.

1233
01:04:18.375 --> 01:04:19.750
Oh, no.

1234
01:04:21.250 --> 01:04:23.125
Bonnie, you don't want them?

1235
01:04:28.417 --> 01:04:31.917
Are you sure? Bonnie? Bonnie?

1236
01:04:32.708 --> 01:04:34.041
I don't know what's come over her.

1237
01:04:34.042 --> 01:04:35.916
I'm so sorry to have bothered you.

1238
01:04:35.917 --> 01:04:37.166
It's all right.

1239
01:04:37.167 --> 01:04:40.249
If you ever change your mind,
Bonnie, just let me know.

1240
01:04:49.667 --> 01:04:51.249
I don't get it. What just happened?

1241
01:04:51.250 --> 01:04:52.708
What is going on, Bonnie?

1242
01:04:53.875 --> 01:04:55.333
Okay, I guess we're going.

1243
01:05:16.667 --> 01:05:19.874
Come on, Bullseye! Quick!
Before they drive away!

1244
01:05:21.792 --> 01:05:23.332
It's… It's too late for me,

1245
01:05:23.333 --> 01:05:25.332
Bullseye, but maybe not for you.

1246
01:05:25.333 --> 01:05:26.999
Please, not for you.

1247
01:05:34.708 --> 01:05:37.291
- Sheriff?
- Jessie? A-Are you okay?

1248
01:05:37.292 --> 01:05:38.791
W-What just happened?

1249
01:05:38.792 --> 01:05:40.374
She ditched you, Jessie.

1250
01:05:40.375 --> 01:05:42.041
Because of you!

1251
01:05:42.042 --> 01:05:44.374
Because of all you darn devices

1252
01:05:44.375 --> 01:05:46.249
making kids act older.

1253
01:05:46.250 --> 01:05:48.291
You stole all our time.

1254
01:05:48.292 --> 01:05:51.166
I wanted to make a difference.
I needed to make a difference.

1255
01:05:51.167 --> 01:05:52.582
And you ruined it.

1256
01:05:52.583 --> 01:05:53.666
Ow.

1257
01:05:53.667 --> 01:05:55.791
- Smarty, you okay?
- I'm-I'm sorry.

1258
01:05:55.792 --> 01:05:59.124
- Are you hurt? Did you crack?
- I'm fine. I'm fine.

1259
01:05:59.125 --> 01:06:01.208
For a rag doll, you throw
quite a punch, cowgir…

1260
01:06:02.083 --> 01:06:03.458
Cowgirl?

1261
01:06:06.542 --> 01:06:07.583
Jessie?

1262
01:06:17.417 --> 01:06:19.166
Uh, Sheriff?

1263
01:06:19.167 --> 01:06:20.916
I'm sorry, Smarty.

1264
01:06:20.917 --> 01:06:22.125
It's not you.

1265
01:06:23.042 --> 01:06:25.291
I'm the one that's useless.

1266
01:06:37.667 --> 01:06:38.958
Bullseye!

1267
01:06:41.500 --> 01:06:44.083
Poor Jessie. Gotta find a way in.

1268
01:06:45.458 --> 01:06:48.166
Buzz. Buzz, where are you going?

1269
01:06:48.167 --> 01:06:50.249
Let's talk about this.

1270
01:06:50.250 --> 01:06:51.958
Huh?

1271
01:06:53.792 --> 01:06:56.416
Uh, what… what is going on?

1272
01:06:56.417 --> 01:06:57.707
- State your name.
- Whoa, whoa.

1273
01:06:57.708 --> 01:06:59.791
- And your purpose.
- Hey, guys.

1274
01:06:59.792 --> 01:07:01.542
- Take him in.
- Guys! Whoa!

1275
01:07:03.250 --> 01:07:05.082
Wait, wait. What's going on?

1276
01:07:05.083 --> 01:07:06.750
My poncho!

1277
01:07:07.250 --> 01:07:08.332
Quiet, assassin!

1278
01:07:08.333 --> 01:07:11.082
Assassin? No, I can't…

1279
01:07:12.250 --> 01:07:13.832
Buzz?

1280
01:07:13.833 --> 01:07:15.957
How do you know who we are? Who sent you?

1281
01:07:15.958 --> 01:07:18.207
Oh, geez! What… I…

1282
01:07:18.208 --> 01:07:20.332
Talk!

1283
01:07:20.333 --> 01:07:22.166
Talk about what?

1284
01:07:22.167 --> 01:07:24.249
- What am I supposed to know?
- You bear a holster.

1285
01:07:24.250 --> 01:07:27.249
You were positioned outside
our leader's stronghold.

1286
01:07:27.250 --> 01:07:29.082
You are an agent of Zurg!

1287
01:07:29.083 --> 01:07:30.666
Zurg? No! Hey!

1288
01:07:30.667 --> 01:07:32.249
I don't even know who your leader is!

1289
01:07:32.250 --> 01:07:34.791
Liar! You wish to harm
the red-haired maiden

1290
01:07:34.792 --> 01:07:36.291
who bears the mark of Star Command.

1291
01:07:36.292 --> 01:07:37.582
- Jessie.
- No.

1292
01:07:37.583 --> 01:07:39.332
Wait!

1293
01:07:39.333 --> 01:07:41.457
He is not an agent of Zurg.

1294
01:07:42.542 --> 01:07:43.832
Well, then, who's this old man?

1295
01:07:43.833 --> 01:07:45.916
Why do people keep saying that?

1296
01:07:45.917 --> 01:07:46.999
I'm not that old!

1297
01:07:47.000 --> 01:07:49.916
This old man is a toy.

1298
01:07:49.917 --> 01:07:51.875
Hmm. A toy?

1299
01:07:52.375 --> 01:07:54.791
Yes. We are all toys!

1300
01:07:54.792 --> 01:07:56.416
Toy…

1301
01:07:56.417 --> 01:07:58.957
Our mission on this planet is
to make a child happy.

1302
01:07:58.958 --> 01:08:00.041
I've been dreaming about that.

1303
01:08:00.042 --> 01:08:01.124
You know what I mean?

1304
01:08:01.125 --> 01:08:03.291
- To play!
- To play. Play.

1305
01:08:03.292 --> 01:08:04.457
Hey! Buzz, can you help me…

1306
01:08:04.458 --> 01:08:06.416
…get out
of the mouth of this pig?

1307
01:08:06.417 --> 01:08:10.041
Search your feelings, Buzz.
You know it to be true!

1308
01:08:12.667 --> 01:08:15.957
And the red-haired maiden
you seek is our toy leader.

1309
01:08:15.958 --> 01:08:17.957
Her name is Sheriff Jessie.

1310
01:08:17.958 --> 01:08:19.041
Sheriff Jessie.

1311
01:08:19.042 --> 01:08:22.291
Sheriff Jessie is trapped
inside that stronghold.

1312
01:08:22.292 --> 01:08:24.499
We must infiltrate it and rescue her

1313
01:08:24.500 --> 01:08:25.749
and her trusty steed.

1314
01:08:25.750 --> 01:08:27.083
How do you know all this?

1315
01:08:27.708 --> 01:08:30.166
Because I am her deputy.

1316
01:08:31.667 --> 01:08:33.124
Star Command.

1317
01:08:33.125 --> 01:08:36.332
Then this old man is a toy?

1318
01:08:36.333 --> 01:08:38.207
This pig has bad breath!

1319
01:08:38.208 --> 01:08:39.374
Oh, yeah, him.

1320
01:08:39.375 --> 01:08:41.499
He's my sidekick. You can untie him.

1321
01:08:41.500 --> 01:08:45.416
And by the way, everybody,
Zurg is our dad.

1322
01:08:45.417 --> 01:08:48.500
- No! No!
- Yeah.

1323
01:08:55.667 --> 01:08:57.458
Hey. What's on your mind?

1324
01:08:57.958 --> 01:08:59.041
I don't know.

1325
01:08:59.042 --> 01:09:00.749
I just hope that girl's okay.

1326
01:09:00.750 --> 01:09:03.374
Aw. She'll be fine, sweetie.

1327
01:09:03.375 --> 01:09:04.582
Don't you worry.

1328
01:09:04.583 --> 01:09:06.832
Hey, guys! Is anyone hungry?

1329
01:09:06.833 --> 01:09:08.249
- Me, me!
- Starving!

1330
01:09:08.250 --> 01:09:09.916
Can we get Pasta Prairie, Baba?

1331
01:09:09.917 --> 01:09:12.375
Ooh, I like
the way you think, anushikes.

1332
01:09:14.583 --> 01:09:16.792
Spread out.

1333
01:09:17.500 --> 01:09:18.625
Not here.

1334
01:09:19.167 --> 01:09:20.499
Not here.

1335
01:09:20.500 --> 01:09:21.542
Definitely not here.

1336
01:09:22.333 --> 01:09:23.999
Blast! Where could she be?

1337
01:09:24.000 --> 01:09:26.499
Commander! We found
these electronic devices.

1338
01:09:26.500 --> 01:09:29.624
Hey, Micro-Chippendales!
Hands off.

1339
01:09:29.625 --> 01:09:31.416
Whoa!

1340
01:09:31.417 --> 01:09:33.457
I'm getting a major signal
from all you dudes.

1341
01:09:33.458 --> 01:09:36.332
- I've got full bars.
- Me too. I can map for miles!

1342
01:09:36.333 --> 01:09:38.249
These guys are their own hot spot.

1343
01:09:39.708 --> 01:09:41.041
Oh, no. They're one of them.

1344
01:09:41.042 --> 01:09:43.832
They're one of us! Nice.

1345
01:09:43.833 --> 01:09:45.332
Hey, uh, this one's broken, by the way.

1346
01:09:45.333 --> 01:09:47.124
Where are you hiding Jessie, you machine?

1347
01:09:47.125 --> 01:09:48.707
Hey, hey. Easy there.

1348
01:09:48.708 --> 01:09:50.332
- Yeah!
- We're Jessie's friends!

1349
01:09:50.333 --> 01:09:52.874
And I have a name. It's Smarty Pants.

1350
01:09:52.875 --> 01:09:54.124
Hygiene instructor.

1351
01:09:54.125 --> 01:09:55.332
He'll wipe your--

1352
01:09:55.333 --> 01:09:57.416
This is serious, Mr. Pants.

1353
01:09:57.417 --> 01:09:59.374
It is my sworn duty as a Space Ranger--

1354
01:09:59.375 --> 01:10:01.499
- Ha, ha, you said "doody."
- Why, you!

1355
01:10:01.500 --> 01:10:03.207
Clearly, we're all friends with Jessie,

1356
01:10:03.208 --> 01:10:05.082
so can you just tell us where she is?

1357
01:10:05.083 --> 01:10:06.582
She went to the tire-swing hill!

1358
01:10:06.583 --> 01:10:07.999
It's at the far end of the ranch.

1359
01:10:08.000 --> 01:10:09.541
Gonna take me forever to waddle there.

1360
01:10:09.542 --> 01:10:11.417
Well, we'll need a way to get there.

1361
01:10:12.125 --> 01:10:13.416
Commander Lightyear.

1362
01:10:15.500 --> 01:10:16.792
Oh, my.

1363
01:10:19.583 --> 01:10:20.833
Whoa.

1364
01:10:30.375 --> 01:10:33.000
Bonnie? Did something happen
with your friends?

1365
01:10:38.458 --> 01:10:39.458
Can you show me?

1366
01:10:41.125 --> 01:10:44.000
You're not in trouble, Bonnie. I promise.

1367
01:10:52.875 --> 01:10:54.083
Oh, sweetie.

1368
01:10:54.667 --> 01:10:58.083
You know that you can always
talk with me and Dad, right?

1369
01:10:58.625 --> 01:11:00.499
About anything.

1370
01:11:00.500 --> 01:11:03.708
Because we love you, Bonnie, so much.

1371
01:11:04.625 --> 01:11:07.417
I wouldn't change
a single thing about you.

1372
01:11:08.083 --> 01:11:10.999
And I think a real friend
would feel the same.

1373
01:11:11.000 --> 01:11:12.000
Don't you?

1374
01:11:13.333 --> 01:11:14.499
But how about we take a break

1375
01:11:14.500 --> 01:11:16.542
from the group chat for now. Okay?

1376
01:11:17.208 --> 01:11:18.417
Let's get some ice cream.

1377
01:11:27.625 --> 01:11:29.374
Trust me, you're gonna love it.

1378
01:11:30.542 --> 01:11:31.750
- Cool!
- Sure.

1379
01:11:43.417 --> 01:11:46.166
Bonnie, they don't have chocolate chip.

1380
01:11:46.167 --> 01:11:47.750
Come pick another flavor.

1381
01:12:09.417 --> 01:12:12.249
Mom, where's Lilypad?

1382
01:12:12.250 --> 01:12:13.958
I'm sorry, Bonnie.

1383
01:12:34.667 --> 01:12:36.124
What is it?

1384
01:12:39.708 --> 01:12:41.041
Bullseye.

1385
01:12:41.042 --> 01:12:42.707
You shouldn't have followed me.

1386
01:12:42.708 --> 01:12:45.292
Oh, bad horse.

1387
01:12:48.958 --> 01:12:52.416
You go back to Blaze's,
Bullseye. You're better off.

1388
01:12:54.625 --> 01:12:58.124
I'm serious. She'll take good care of you.

1389
01:12:58.125 --> 01:12:59.666
And all those horses…

1390
01:13:03.333 --> 01:13:05.416
Bullseye, no.

1391
01:13:05.417 --> 01:13:07.083
I'm not going with you.

1392
01:13:07.583 --> 01:13:09.291
I…

1393
01:13:09.292 --> 01:13:11.457
can't do this again.

1394
01:13:11.458 --> 01:13:12.458
I can't…

1395
01:13:13.625 --> 01:13:15.291
love another kid

1396
01:13:15.292 --> 01:13:17.958
just to find out I never mattered.

1397
01:13:19.667 --> 01:13:20.542
I…

1398
01:13:21.333 --> 01:13:22.958
I can't.

1399
01:13:40.875 --> 01:13:43.583
I didn't write that.

1400
01:13:44.417 --> 01:13:45.917
It must have been…

1401
01:14:02.500 --> 01:14:03.667
Emily?

1402
01:14:06.583 --> 01:14:09.166
Daffodil, dig.

1403
01:14:26.083 --> 01:14:27.125
Wait.

1404
01:14:28.375 --> 01:14:30.541
This ain't stuff from Emily.

1405
01:14:30.542 --> 01:14:31.542
It…

1406
01:14:32.167 --> 01:14:33.292
It's newer.

1407
01:14:36.000 --> 01:14:37.249
It doesn't make any sense.

1408
01:14:37.250 --> 01:14:39.457
She wouldn't have any of this stuff.

1409
01:14:39.458 --> 01:14:40.958
She'd be…

1410
01:14:44.333 --> 01:14:46.166
all grown-up.

1411
01:14:49.542 --> 01:14:50.542
Wait.

1412
01:14:57.375 --> 01:15:00.167
Emily named her daughter…

1413
01:15:04.083 --> 01:15:05.500
after me.

1414
01:15:15.333 --> 01:15:16.667
Really?

1415
01:15:32.375 --> 01:15:33.791
Uh…

1416
01:15:33.792 --> 01:15:35.749
Whoa!

1417
01:15:40.333 --> 01:15:41.749
Jessie? Bullseye!

1418
01:15:41.750 --> 01:15:43.041
Hey, I found 'em!

1419
01:15:43.042 --> 01:15:44.083
Woody?

1420
01:15:45.042 --> 01:15:46.832
- Buzz!
- Jessie!

1421
01:15:47.792 --> 01:15:48.957
You're okay.

1422
01:15:48.958 --> 01:15:51.041
What… What are you doing here?

1423
01:15:51.042 --> 01:15:52.666
We came for you, Jessie.

1424
01:15:52.667 --> 01:15:53.791
For me?

1425
01:15:53.792 --> 01:15:55.250
We all did.

1426
01:16:03.958 --> 01:16:06.916
Well, howdy-do, Sheriff?

1427
01:16:06.917 --> 01:16:08.291
We come bearing Buzzes.

1428
01:16:08.292 --> 01:16:10.791
Looks like 50 to me,
but I can only count to two.

1429
01:16:13.083 --> 01:16:15.499
Star Command. Star Command.
Star Command. Star Command.

1430
01:16:15.500 --> 01:16:17.542
Star Command. Star
Command. Star Command.

1431
01:16:18.083 --> 01:16:19.499
Star Command.

1432
01:16:19.500 --> 01:16:21.624
All right, all right, calm down.

1433
01:16:21.625 --> 01:16:22.832
Give her some room, fellas.

1434
01:16:22.833 --> 01:16:24.874
- Uh, Buzz.
- Yes?

1435
01:16:24.875 --> 01:16:27.500
Hey, hey, she meant that for me. Just me.

1436
01:16:28.125 --> 01:16:30.457
- We saw Bonnie give you away.
- You did?

1437
01:16:30.458 --> 01:16:31.957
It doesn't make any sense.

1438
01:16:31.958 --> 01:16:33.291
You're not useless, Sheriff!

1439
01:16:33.292 --> 01:16:35.374
- We love you!
- So much!

1440
01:16:43.208 --> 01:16:44.583
Look, I'm okay.

1441
01:16:45.250 --> 01:16:48.000
Bonnie's growing up.

1442
01:16:49.208 --> 01:16:54.292
And we don't get to decide
when and how that happens.

1443
01:16:55.542 --> 01:16:57.041
All that matters is

1444
01:16:57.042 --> 01:16:59.082
we were there at the right time

1445
01:16:59.083 --> 01:17:00.832
to help her along.

1446
01:17:07.625 --> 01:17:09.708
And I gotta believe we were.

1447
01:17:10.875 --> 01:17:12.999
You make us proud to be toys, Jessie.

1448
01:17:13.000 --> 01:17:14.624
What are you doing? Stop!

1449
01:17:14.625 --> 01:17:16.707
Sorry, guys. Sorry.

1450
01:17:17.792 --> 01:17:20.708
Just wish she had at least
connected with Blaze.

1451
01:17:21.667 --> 01:17:22.999
Wait.

1452
01:17:23.000 --> 01:17:25.249
Connect! They still can!

1453
01:17:25.250 --> 01:17:26.832
Lilypad can do that!

1454
01:17:26.833 --> 01:17:28.083
- Lilypad?
- Lilypad?

1455
01:17:36.583 --> 01:17:38.332
Okay, okay. Guys, message coming through.

1456
01:17:38.333 --> 01:17:40.332
"Jessie, I'm so sorry.

1457
01:17:40.333 --> 01:17:42.416
Chose wrong friends. Hurt Bonnie."

1458
01:17:42.417 --> 01:17:43.624
- Oh, no.
- Bonnie.

1459
01:17:43.625 --> 01:17:46.167
Smarty, send a reply. "You can fix it."

1460
01:17:51.583 --> 01:17:54.291
"No, I can't. Threw myself away."

1461
01:17:54.292 --> 01:17:55.999
- What?
- "On donation truck."

1462
01:17:56.000 --> 01:17:59.416
Jumpin' Jehoshaphat!
Now she throws herself away?

1463
01:17:59.417 --> 01:18:01.291
We're goin' after her.

1464
01:18:01.292 --> 01:18:02.582
- What?
- But how?

1465
01:18:02.583 --> 01:18:05.917
Smarty, tell Lily to send
a photo of where she is.

1466
01:18:06.667 --> 01:18:07.749
Got it.

1467
01:18:07.750 --> 01:18:09.707
Snappy, zoom in on that blurry road sign.

1468
01:18:09.708 --> 01:18:11.582
Look at you with that tech talk, cowgirl.

1469
01:18:11.583 --> 01:18:12.874
Martin Avenue.

1470
01:18:12.875 --> 01:18:14.457
Atlas, can you get us to that truck?

1471
01:18:14.458 --> 01:18:16.374
Already mapped it, cowboy lady.

1472
01:18:16.375 --> 01:18:18.749
Tell Lily to keep sending
photos of where she is.

1473
01:18:18.750 --> 01:18:20.166
We're getting her back.

1474
01:18:20.167 --> 01:18:21.582
Yes, Sheriff.

1475
01:18:21.583 --> 01:18:23.166
Jessie, when you have a moment,

1476
01:18:23.167 --> 01:18:24.541
there's something you'd like to ask me…

1477
01:18:24.542 --> 01:18:26.624
- I'd like to ask you.
- Sure thing, Deputy.

1478
01:18:26.625 --> 01:18:28.583
- Now, a little help?
- Yes, Sheriff.

1479
01:18:29.792 --> 01:18:31.624
Yeehaw!

1480
01:18:31.625 --> 01:18:33.166
Let's ride.

1481
01:18:34.500 --> 01:18:36.250
Whoa! Hey!

1482
01:18:38.833 --> 01:18:40.624
- Hey! Hey, wait for us!
- Hey! Wait for us!

1483
01:18:54.417 --> 01:18:56.291
She's not far.

1484
01:18:56.292 --> 01:18:59.249
If we go south five blocks,
then east for two,

1485
01:18:59.250 --> 01:19:00.249
we might be able to head 'em off

1486
01:19:00.250 --> 01:19:01.166
before they reach the highway.

1487
01:19:01.167 --> 01:19:02.249
Car!

1488
01:19:05.542 --> 01:19:07.208
Clear!

1489
01:19:07.708 --> 01:19:08.916
She just passed a gas station.

1490
01:19:08.917 --> 01:19:11.249
Passed gas. Sorry, had to.

1491
01:19:11.250 --> 01:19:12.874
We're close. Take a shortcut.

1492
01:19:12.875 --> 01:19:14.208
Down this next road to the right.

1493
01:19:19.417 --> 01:19:20.332
It's a house!

1494
01:19:20.333 --> 01:19:21.749
I don't get it. There should be a road.

1495
01:19:21.750 --> 01:19:24.082
Probably was a road
five years ago. Old map.

1496
01:19:24.083 --> 01:19:26.416
- Recalculating.
- No time. We're going through.

1497
01:19:26.417 --> 01:19:28.000
- Wait, what?
- Going through?

1498
01:19:36.792 --> 01:19:37.750
Down, boy, down!

1499
01:19:39.625 --> 01:19:41.541
Whoa, whoa.

1500
01:19:45.167 --> 01:19:46.582
Yeehaw!

1501
01:19:57.000 --> 01:20:00.124
The truck. I see it up ahead.

1502
01:20:01.625 --> 01:20:02.957
Follow me.

1503
01:20:02.958 --> 01:20:04.042
Yes, Sheriff.

1504
01:20:13.000 --> 01:20:13.916
Whoo!

1505
01:20:13.917 --> 01:20:15.999
We have reached our destination.

1506
01:20:16.000 --> 01:20:17.291
- Lily?
- Lily!

1507
01:20:17.292 --> 01:20:19.207
- Lily, where are ya?
- Lily!

1508
01:20:19.208 --> 01:20:20.791
- Lily?
- Lilypad, where you at?

1509
01:20:20.792 --> 01:20:22.082
Hey, Lily.

1510
01:20:22.083 --> 01:20:23.333
Yes, can I help you?

1511
01:20:24.875 --> 01:20:27.874
Lily. It's okay. We got ya.

1512
01:20:27.875 --> 01:20:29.166
You shouldn't have come, Jessie.

1513
01:20:29.167 --> 01:20:31.249
Nuh-uh. No time for pity parties, Lily.

1514
01:20:31.250 --> 01:20:33.499
Bonnie still needs you to make a friend.

1515
01:20:33.500 --> 01:20:34.458
Me? But I…

1516
01:20:35.458 --> 01:20:38.832
I made a major miscalculation
with Kara, Chelsea and Heidi.

1517
01:20:38.833 --> 01:20:40.749
You were right. Bonnie's different.

1518
01:20:40.750 --> 01:20:41.707
She deserves better.

1519
01:20:41.708 --> 01:20:42.791
Lily.

1520
01:20:42.792 --> 01:20:45.207
You didn't know those girls
were wrong for Bonnie.

1521
01:20:45.208 --> 01:20:46.791
No, I'm wrong for Bonnie.

1522
01:20:46.792 --> 01:20:49.832
- I'm the one who caused this.
- Well, then help me fix it.

1523
01:20:49.833 --> 01:20:52.082
I found Bonnie the right friend.

1524
01:20:52.083 --> 01:20:53.291
- You did?
- Yep.

1525
01:20:53.292 --> 01:20:55.541
So, how about you and me connect them?

1526
01:20:55.542 --> 01:20:57.457
Uh… Okay.

1527
01:20:57.458 --> 01:20:59.707
But first, we gotta get
everyone off this truck

1528
01:20:59.708 --> 01:21:00.832
and back home.

1529
01:21:05.750 --> 01:21:08.416
Uh, we are moving way too fast
to get off now.

1530
01:21:08.417 --> 01:21:10.916
And we're going farther away
by the second.

1531
01:21:10.917 --> 01:21:12.916
There's gotta be something we can do.

1532
01:21:12.917 --> 01:21:15.124
We've got all these fancy Buzzes.

1533
01:21:17.750 --> 01:21:19.582
Excuse me. Move, move. Out of the way.

1534
01:21:19.583 --> 01:21:20.833
Spaceman, turn around.

1535
01:21:29.042 --> 01:21:31.541
- Snap!
- Yes, yes, yes, yes!

1536
01:21:31.542 --> 01:21:32.916
No way.

1537
01:21:32.917 --> 01:21:34.957
Oh, yeah. Way.

1538
01:21:39.625 --> 01:21:40.916
Ready, Sheriff?

1539
01:21:40.917 --> 01:21:42.125
Punch it, Lily.

1540
01:21:56.583 --> 01:21:58.499
Whoa.

1541
01:21:58.500 --> 01:22:00.666
Fly. Be free!

1542
01:22:00.667 --> 01:22:01.667
Show-offs!

1543
01:22:09.375 --> 01:22:11.207
Wow.

1544
01:22:11.208 --> 01:22:12.625
Whoo-hoo!

1545
01:22:13.208 --> 01:22:14.542
- Whoo!
- Whoo!

1546
01:22:16.250 --> 01:22:18.332
Now, this is flying.

1547
01:22:18.333 --> 01:22:19.541
With style!

1548
01:22:19.542 --> 01:22:22.208
Yeehaw!

1549
01:22:27.542 --> 01:22:29.041
So, we're clear on the plan?

1550
01:22:29.042 --> 01:22:31.207
Once you're at Bonnie's,
you send the message.

1551
01:22:31.208 --> 01:22:33.207
Blaze brings me and Bullseye to the house,

1552
01:22:33.208 --> 01:22:35.582
and this time, they connect!

1553
01:22:35.583 --> 01:22:37.791
Jessie, wait.
What if Bonnie rejects you again?

1554
01:22:37.792 --> 01:22:40.499
If they become friends, it's all worth it.

1555
01:22:40.500 --> 01:22:42.000
Yes, Sheriff.

1556
01:22:43.125 --> 01:22:46.166
Huh? Wait. Jessie, wait!

1557
01:22:46.167 --> 01:22:47.250
What?

1558
01:22:48.750 --> 01:22:49.999
What is it, Buzz?

1559
01:22:50.000 --> 01:22:51.207
Just listen to me.

1560
01:22:51.208 --> 01:22:53.249
I… I've been trying
to ask you this, and if…

1561
01:22:53.250 --> 01:22:55.707
if I don't do it now, I never will.

1562
01:22:55.708 --> 01:22:57.708
Will you…

1563
01:22:58.208 --> 01:23:00.499
Buzz, you can do this.

1564
01:23:00.500 --> 01:23:01.833
Will… Will…

1565
01:23:08.000 --> 01:23:10.333
You're stuck with me, Deputy.

1566
01:23:16.042 --> 01:23:17.999
Cheer up, boys. She'll be back.

1567
01:23:18.000 --> 01:23:19.417
We have a plan!

1568
01:23:19.917 --> 01:23:22.624
At ease, Ranger. At ease.

1569
01:23:43.125 --> 01:23:44.666
Men, you know your mission.

1570
01:23:44.667 --> 01:23:45.667
Yes, Commander.

1571
01:23:50.292 --> 01:23:51.624
Woody! Buzz!

1572
01:23:51.625 --> 01:23:53.124
- What?
- Lily!

1573
01:23:53.125 --> 01:23:54.624
- Oh, no, no, no.
- Foul device.

1574
01:23:54.625 --> 01:23:55.916
What's she doing here?

1575
01:23:55.917 --> 01:23:57.499
She's one of us, guys. Deal with it.

1576
01:23:57.500 --> 01:23:58.582
Listen up, everyone.

1577
01:23:58.583 --> 01:24:00.791
Lily and Jessie
have a plan to help Bonnie.

1578
01:24:00.792 --> 01:24:02.624
Okay, what do you need us to do?

1579
01:24:02.625 --> 01:24:03.582
Nothing.

1580
01:24:03.583 --> 01:24:05.457
- Nothing?
- That's easy.

1581
01:24:05.458 --> 01:24:07.166
Jessie already did the hard work.

1582
01:24:07.167 --> 01:24:08.332
Classic Jessica.

1583
01:24:08.333 --> 01:24:11.375
All that's left for me
is to send a message.

1584
01:24:29.417 --> 01:24:31.167
It's up to the girls now.

1585
01:24:51.958 --> 01:24:54.541
Hey, sweetie.
Look what I found in the car.

1586
01:24:55.500 --> 01:24:57.707
It's okay. We turned off the chat.

1587
01:25:14.375 --> 01:25:16.832
Bonnie. You have a friend at the door.

1588
01:25:18.792 --> 01:25:20.249
- Let's try to beat…
- Hi, Bonnie.

1589
01:25:20.250 --> 01:25:22.250
- …our high score.
- I brought your dolls.

1590
01:25:24.000 --> 01:25:25.791
Bonnie, come say hi.

1591
01:25:25.792 --> 01:25:26.833
Okay.

1592
01:25:35.417 --> 01:25:36.458
Hi.

1593
01:25:37.292 --> 01:25:38.292
Hi.

1594
01:25:46.042 --> 01:25:47.999
I'm sorry. I don't play with toys--

1595
01:25:48.000 --> 01:25:49.667
I played with her a little yesterday.

1596
01:25:50.500 --> 01:25:52.124
I like it when she's like,

1597
01:25:52.125 --> 01:25:54.042
"I ain't afraid of nothin', partner."

1598
01:26:00.750 --> 01:26:02.792
That… That was weird.

1599
01:26:03.292 --> 01:26:04.833
Uh… I…

1600
01:26:05.500 --> 01:26:06.583
Sorry I bothered you.

1601
01:26:11.583 --> 01:26:13.124
- Oh, no. Don't go.
- No, no, no.

1602
01:26:13.125 --> 01:26:14.667
- She can't go. She can't go.
- No, no, no, no.

1603
01:26:16.583 --> 01:26:17.625
Blaze!

1604
01:26:31.167 --> 01:26:34.292
I like your boots.

1605
01:26:37.875 --> 01:26:40.125
I… I really like your socks.

1606
01:26:42.833 --> 01:26:45.625
Do you like my beard, madame?

1607
01:26:46.333 --> 01:26:49.041
Very impressive, m'lady.

1608
01:26:49.042 --> 01:26:51.749
Yes, I'm one billion years old.

1609
01:26:51.750 --> 01:26:53.750
That's why it's so glorious.

1610
01:27:01.458 --> 01:27:02.791
Um…

1611
01:27:02.792 --> 01:27:04.375
Do you wanna play?

1612
01:27:06.792 --> 01:27:07.792
Okay.

1613
01:27:08.875 --> 01:27:10.291
- Walter, let's go.
- Okay. Okay.

1614
01:27:10.292 --> 01:27:12.166
- Do you actually have a horse?
- Yeah.

1615
01:27:12.167 --> 01:27:13.666
Like, a real one?

1616
01:27:13.667 --> 01:27:15.250
Yes! It's real.

1617
01:27:17.917 --> 01:27:20.499
Hey, I have an idea.

1618
01:27:30.958 --> 01:27:32.542
Look at that kilt.

1619
01:27:43.292 --> 01:27:45.792
Please, take care of my son.

1620
01:27:50.792 --> 01:27:53.874
Friends, we are gathered here today

1621
01:27:53.875 --> 01:27:57.207
to witness the most wonderfulest union

1622
01:27:57.208 --> 01:27:58.624
of Sheriff Jessie

1623
01:27:58.625 --> 01:28:01.374
and Buzz-tholomew MacLightyear.

1624
01:28:09.417 --> 01:28:10.707
Now, Sheriff,

1625
01:28:10.708 --> 01:28:14.582
please put this ring
onto Buzz's itty-bitty finger

1626
01:28:14.583 --> 01:28:16.375
and make your vows.

1627
01:28:17.875 --> 01:28:20.457
Buzz, will you take this ring

1628
01:28:20.458 --> 01:28:22.166
as my pinky promise

1629
01:28:22.167 --> 01:28:25.207
to have fun, and play with you and stuff,

1630
01:28:25.208 --> 01:28:27.166
for all my days,

1631
01:28:27.167 --> 01:28:29.207
even the hard ones?

1632
01:28:29.208 --> 01:28:31.125
- I do--
- Bonnie…

1633
01:28:31.750 --> 01:28:33.374
have you seen my wedding ring?

1634
01:28:34.292 --> 01:28:35.666
Uh…

1635
01:28:35.667 --> 01:28:37.707
Maybe check the bathroom?

1636
01:28:37.708 --> 01:28:39.082
Wait, wait, wait. We need, like…

1637
01:28:39.083 --> 01:28:40.332
Flowers! From the garden.

1638
01:28:40.333 --> 01:28:41.750
- Good idea.
- Follow me.

1639
01:28:42.417 --> 01:28:44.500
And there's confetti in the craft drawer.

1640
01:28:45.625 --> 01:28:47.041
Oh, congrats, you two.

1641
01:28:47.042 --> 01:28:48.541
Don't worry. I took plenty of photos

1642
01:28:48.542 --> 01:28:49.707
for Smarty and the gang.

1643
01:28:49.708 --> 01:28:52.417
That's really sweet of you, Lily.

1644
01:28:54.042 --> 01:28:55.042
Mmm.

1645
01:28:55.625 --> 01:28:57.042
You done good, Sheriff.

1646
01:28:57.833 --> 01:28:59.750
You can call me Jessica.

1647
01:29:00.292 --> 01:29:01.917
Okay, I will. Jessica.

1648
01:29:02.625 --> 01:29:04.166
Actually, no. No.

1649
01:29:04.167 --> 01:29:05.249
Okay.

1650
01:29:06.417 --> 01:29:07.749
Hey, when you get a chance,

1651
01:29:07.750 --> 01:29:10.207
can you introduce me to the ring bearer?

1652
01:29:10.208 --> 01:29:11.874
- Oh.
- Awooga.

1653
01:29:11.875 --> 01:29:12.999
Okay.

1654
01:29:13.000 --> 01:29:14.083
They're coming.

1655
01:29:15.000 --> 01:29:16.457
I got it. That's awesome.

1656
01:29:16.458 --> 01:29:17.916
That's such a good idea.

1657
01:29:17.917 --> 01:29:19.791
The wedding is on.

1658
01:29:19.792 --> 01:29:20.874
Okay!

1659
01:29:20.875 --> 01:29:22.291
- Buzz…
- Buzz,

1660
01:29:22.292 --> 01:29:25.332
do you take me as
your super cool, sheriff wife?

1661
01:29:25.333 --> 01:29:26.707
I do.

1662
01:29:26.708 --> 01:29:28.207
And do you take me as your handsome,

1663
01:29:28.208 --> 01:29:30.375
Space Ranger husband?

1664
01:29:30.917 --> 01:29:32.500
Oh.

1665
01:29:33.250 --> 01:29:34.500
I do.

1666
01:29:35.208 --> 01:29:37.332
Then I now pronounce you--

1667
01:29:37.333 --> 01:29:39.249
I object!

1668
01:29:39.250 --> 01:29:40.167
Oh, no.

1669
01:29:40.958 --> 01:29:43.041
Buzz is already married…

1670
01:29:43.042 --> 01:29:44.166
to me!

1671
01:29:47.750 --> 01:29:51.207
This is the third time
this has happened to me!

1672
01:29:51.208 --> 01:29:52.666
How could you?

1673
01:29:52.667 --> 01:29:53.707
Slap.

1674
01:29:53.708 --> 01:29:56.374
Jessie, it's not what you think.

1675
01:29:56.375 --> 01:29:59.207
Tell them, Buzz! Tell them about our love!

1676
01:29:59.208 --> 01:30:01.291
But, Trixie, that was then…

1677
01:30:01.292 --> 01:30:03.833
…and this is now.

1678
01:30:04.500 --> 01:30:05.582
Protect the babies!

1679
01:30:05.583 --> 01:30:07.124
You'll hear from my lawyers about this!

1680
01:30:07.125 --> 01:30:08.791
- This is an outrage.
- Tell them, Buzz.

1681
01:30:08.792 --> 01:30:11.583
- Congratulations.
- You got this, Deputy.

1682
01:30:12.667 --> 01:30:14.332
- So did you help?
- Yeah.

1683
01:30:14.333 --> 01:30:16.207
We just followed Jessie's lead.

1684
01:30:16.208 --> 01:30:18.416
- Woody, will you…
- Um…

1685
01:30:18.417 --> 01:30:20.833
- …hold these? I'll drive.
- Well…

1686
01:30:21.875 --> 01:30:23.000
Ooh, la la.

1687
01:30:27.000 --> 01:30:29.166
- Yes! Oh, look at them.
- They're glowing.

1688
01:30:29.167 --> 01:30:30.624
They're such good friends.

1689
01:30:30.625 --> 01:30:31.957
Okay, save that one.

1690
01:30:31.958 --> 01:30:33.374
- Fierce.
- Oh, my gosh. Yes!

1691
01:30:33.375 --> 01:30:34.416
Okay, Buzz with the kilt.

1692
01:30:34.417 --> 01:30:36.374
I'm moving to Palm Springs.

1693
01:30:36.375 --> 01:30:38.166
What if Trixie
poisoned the wedding cake?

1694
01:30:38.167 --> 01:30:41.708
But, Trixie, why?

1695
01:30:42.250 --> 01:30:44.624
Hey, would you ever wanna sleep over?

1696
01:30:44.625 --> 01:30:47.458
Yes! That'd be so fun.

1697
01:30:47.958 --> 01:30:49.083
Look. Look, look.

1698
01:30:51.292 --> 01:30:53.499
Friends forever, partner.

1699
01:30:53.500 --> 01:30:56.666
Come on, Jessie.
We'll take my spaceship.

1700
01:30:56.667 --> 01:30:58.707
- Where to first?
- Neptune!

1701
01:30:58.708 --> 01:30:59.916
What are you guys doing?

1702
01:30:59.917 --> 01:31:01.416
Honeymooning!

1703
01:31:01.417 --> 01:31:02.499
Wanna come?

1704
01:31:02.500 --> 01:31:05.082
- Sure!
- Wait, wait.

1705
01:31:05.083 --> 01:31:06.582
Look, Jessie, space dolphins!

1706
01:31:06.583 --> 01:31:07.666
Hi, dolphin.

1707
01:31:29.625 --> 01:31:31.874
♪ I knew you ♪

1708
01:31:31.875 --> 01:31:33.916
♪ Through the daze
Of the blades of the grass ♪

1709
01:31:33.917 --> 01:31:35.166
♪ In summer ♪

1710
01:31:35.167 --> 01:31:37.041
♪ Parachutes ♪

1711
01:31:37.042 --> 01:31:39.416
♪ For the free fall
Of being younger ♪

1712
01:31:39.417 --> 01:31:44.667
♪ I memorized the sound
Of your bare footsteps ♪

1713
01:31:45.708 --> 01:31:48.124
♪ Running wild ♪

1714
01:31:48.125 --> 01:31:49.750
♪ It's been a long time ♪

1715
01:31:50.917 --> 01:31:55.125
♪ Life has ways
Of leaving those days behind ♪

1716
01:31:55.917 --> 01:31:58.957
♪ But seeing you tonight ♪

1717
01:31:58.958 --> 01:32:00.916
♪ I remembered I loved you ♪

1718
01:32:00.917 --> 01:32:03.207
♪ Came back when it mattered
I saw you ♪

1719
01:32:03.208 --> 01:32:05.749
♪ Standing there
In the light of the window ♪

1720
01:32:05.750 --> 01:32:07.416
♪ Wearing that same smile ♪

1721
01:32:07.417 --> 01:32:09.207
♪ Man, it's been a while ♪

1722
01:32:09.208 --> 01:32:10.875
♪ But I knew it, I knew you ♪

1723
01:32:13.208 --> 01:32:15.208
♪ I knew it, I knew you ♪

1724
01:32:16.083 --> 01:32:18.374
♪ I knew you ♪

1725
01:32:18.375 --> 01:32:19.457
♪ All your blues ♪

1726
01:32:19.458 --> 01:32:21.624
♪ Like a mood ring
Changing colors ♪

1727
01:32:21.625 --> 01:32:23.499
♪ You did too ♪

1728
01:32:23.500 --> 01:32:25.666
♪ There were times
We could fight like brothers ♪

1729
01:32:25.667 --> 01:32:30.374
♪ I watched you drive
Around the bend ♪

1730
01:32:30.375 --> 01:32:32.916
♪ For what
I thought would be ♪

1731
01:32:32.917 --> 01:32:36.167
♪ The last time
I saw my friend ♪

1732
01:32:37.083 --> 01:32:40.166
♪ But love has ways
Of bringing things back ♪

1733
01:32:40.167 --> 01:32:41.917
♪ To life ♪

1734
01:32:42.500 --> 01:32:45.291
♪ All you said was hi ♪

1735
01:32:45.292 --> 01:32:47.374
♪ And I remembered
I loved you ♪

1736
01:32:47.375 --> 01:32:49.832
♪ Came back when it mattered
I saw you ♪

1737
01:32:49.833 --> 01:32:52.207
♪ Standing there
In the light of the window ♪

1738
01:32:52.208 --> 01:32:53.874
♪ Wearing that same smile ♪

1739
01:32:53.875 --> 01:32:55.624
♪ Man, it's been a while ♪

1740
01:32:55.625 --> 01:32:57.707
♪ But I knew it, I knew you ♪

1741
01:32:57.708 --> 01:32:59.167
♪ I knew ♪

1742
01:33:00.292 --> 01:33:04.167
- ♪ I knew, I knew ♪
- ♪ I knew it, I knew you ♪

1743
01:33:05.625 --> 01:33:08.000
- ♪ I knew, I knew ♪
- ♪ I knew it, I knew you ♪

1744
01:33:18.375 --> 01:33:20.916
♪ Oh the rivers I cried ♪

1745
01:33:20.917 --> 01:33:22.750
♪ When we said goodbye ♪

1746
01:33:23.792 --> 01:33:28.499
♪ Wondering if I'd made it up
In my mind ♪

1747
01:33:28.500 --> 01:33:31.417
♪ And now you looked me
In the eye ♪

1748
01:33:31.917 --> 01:33:33.832
♪ And you told me
I loved you ♪

1749
01:33:33.833 --> 01:33:36.249
♪ Came back when it mattered
I saw you ♪

1750
01:33:36.250 --> 01:33:38.666
♪ Standing there
In the light of the window ♪

1751
01:33:38.667 --> 01:33:40.291
♪ Wearing that same smile ♪

1752
01:33:40.292 --> 01:33:42.000
♪ Yeah, it's been a while ♪

1753
01:33:43.833 --> 01:33:45.332
♪ Wearing that same smile ♪

1754
01:33:45.333 --> 01:33:47.082
♪ Man, it's been a while ♪

1755
01:33:47.083 --> 01:33:48.999
♪ Been a while ♪

1756
01:33:49.000 --> 01:33:50.624
♪ Wearing that same smile ♪

1757
01:33:50.625 --> 01:33:52.416
♪ Man, it's been a while ♪

1758
01:33:52.417 --> 01:33:54.457
♪ But I knew it, I knew you ♪

1759
01:33:54.458 --> 01:33:56.458
♪ I knew you ♪

1760
01:33:57.042 --> 01:33:59.666
- ♪ I knew ♪
- ♪ I knew it, I knew you ♪

1761
01:33:59.667 --> 01:34:01.292
♪ I knew you ♪

1762
01:34:01.875 --> 01:34:03.792
♪ Wearing that same smile ♪

1763
01:34:05.458 --> 01:34:07.625
♪ I knew it, I knew you ♪

1764
01:34:10.625 --> 01:34:12.333
♪ I knew it, I knew you ♪

1765
01:34:13.167 --> 01:34:14.167
♪ I knew it! ♪

1766
01:34:26.708 --> 01:34:27.708
Whoa!

1767
01:34:35.708 --> 01:34:36.833
Huh?

1768
01:34:45.167 --> 01:34:46.624
I am Buzz Lightyear.

1769
01:34:46.625 --> 01:34:48.666
To infinity and beyond!

1770
01:35:02.708 --> 01:35:04.791
Hey! You kids play nice. I--

1771
01:35:04.792 --> 01:35:05.792
Oh.

1772
01:35:10.375 --> 01:35:11.666
Mission accomplished.

1773
01:35:16.208 --> 01:35:18.666
We meet again, my son.

1774
01:35:18.667 --> 01:35:20.208
No!

1775
01:40:11.583 --> 01:40:14.082
- I don't know how to do this.
- Drop the beat.

1776
01:40:14.083 --> 01:40:15.624
- ♪ Hey ♪
- ♪ Me and the toys ♪

1777
01:40:15.625 --> 01:40:16.749
- ♪ Me and the toys ♪
- ♪ Make a friend ♪

1778
01:40:16.750 --> 01:40:18.291
- ♪ Toys ♪
- I can't do this.

1779
01:40:18.292 --> 01:40:19.957
♪ Try to get Bonnie
To make a friend ♪

1780
01:40:19.958 --> 01:40:21.374
- ♪ All summer ♪
- ♪ All summer ♪

1781
01:40:21.375 --> 01:40:22.999
♪ Me and the toys
Been workin' ♪

1782
01:40:23.000 --> 01:40:24.874
- ♪ Been workin' all summer! ♪
- ♪ Make a friend ♪

1783
01:40:24.875 --> 01:40:26.207
- ♪ Hey, yeah ♪
- ♪ Make a friend ♪

1784
01:40:26.208 --> 01:40:27.375
What does it even mean?

1785
01:40:28.292 --> 01:40:30.249
♪ Hey, hey
Me and the toys ♪

1786
01:40:30.250 --> 01:40:32.041
♪ Me and the toys been
Workin' all summer ♪

1787
01:40:32.042 --> 01:40:33.291
♪ Try to get Bonnie
To make a friend ♪

1788
01:40:33.292 --> 01:40:34.666
- ♪ Toys ♪
- ♪ Make a friend ♪

1789
01:40:34.667 --> 01:40:35.582
♪ All summer ♪

1790
01:40:35.583 --> 01:40:36.874
It needs a melody.

1791
01:40:36.875 --> 01:40:37.957
Make it stop.

1792
01:40:37.958 --> 01:40:39.542
Pizza con gafas, baby.

1793
01:40:40.042 --> 01:40:42.958
I am not a chair!

